window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b009-fd16a0c043261114.json"]={sha256:"fd16a0c043261114355db0b55cb50f3ef52e10c4c24243d92059be54a9ac90c7",value:{"id":"b009","title":"昂船洲大橋","titleEn":"Stonecutters Bridge","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"昂船洲大橋以 1,018 m 主跨橫越香港藍巴勒海峽，主跨為中央開槽的流線形雙鋼箱梁，背跨為預力混凝土雙箱梁，兩座單柱塔下段為混凝土、上段為雙相不鏽鋼外皮的鋼—混凝土複合結構。本課從颱風風荷載、塔梁液壓緩衝器、224 根斜拉索、鋼箱梁吊裝與鋼混接頭，一路到雷諾數效應的風洞試驗、跨中撓度監測與長索維護。","summaryEn":"Stonecutters Bridge crosses Hong Kong’s Rambler Channel with a 1,018 m main span of streamlined twin steel boxes separated by a central gap, prestressed concrete twin-box back spans and two monopole towers whose lower parts are concrete and upper parts steel–concrete composite with a duplex stainless skin. The course runs from typhoon wind load, tower–deck hydraulic buffers, the 224 stays, deck-segment lifting and the steel–concrete junction to Reynolds-number effects in wind testing, mid-span deflection monitoring and long-stay maintenance.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-cable-stayed","subcategoryTitle":"斜張橋與斜索系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Cable-stayed bridges and stay systems","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-cable-stayed","learningTags":["structures","st-cable-stayed","cablestayed"],"architectureFamily":"cablestayed","architectureNodes":[["不鏽鋼複合單柱塔","Composite stainless monopole towers"],["224 根斜拉索與錨箱","224 stays and anchor boxes"],["分離式雙鋼箱主梁","Split twin steel-box main span"],["混凝土背跨與鋼混接頭","Concrete back spans and steel–concrete junction"],["塔梁液壓緩衝器","Tower–deck hydraulic buffers"],["風與結構健康監測","Wind and structural health monitoring"]],"architectureEdges":[[2,1],[1,0],[1,3],[2,3],[2,4],[4,0],[2,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"cablestayed","labels":["不鏽鋼複合單柱塔","224 根斜拉索與錨箱","分離式雙鋼箱主梁","混凝土背跨與鋼混接頭","塔梁液壓緩衝器"],"labelsEn":["Composite stainless monopole towers","224 stays and anchor boxes","Split twin steel-box main span","Concrete back spans and steel–concrete junction","Tower–deck hydraulic buffers"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：估算颱風時主跨跨中的側向變形量級。取橋面側風荷載 w = 4.9 kN/m（U = 50 m/s、C_D = 0.8、D = 4 m），主跨 L = 1,018 m。若把主跨視為兩端由塔約束、中間由斜索提供有限側向勁度的梁，以簡支梁上限估計 δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI)：取兩箱合計側向 EI = 2.0×10¹⁰ kN·m²，L⁴ = 1,018⁴ ≈ 1.074×10¹²，δ = 5×4.9×1.074×10¹²/(384×2.0×10¹⁰) ≈ 2.63×10¹³/7.68×10¹² ≈ 3.4 m。公開資料中風荷載跨中撓度約 2.2 m，比簡支上限小，表示斜索的擺錘效應與塔的約束分擔了約 35% 的側向變形（1 − 2.2/3.4 ≈ 0.35）。若風速降為 40 m/s，w 與 δ 都乘以 (40/50)² = 0.64。EI 與係數為教學假設，非本橋設計值。","textEn":"Design exercise: estimate the order of mid-span lateral movement in a typhoon. Take a side wind load w = 4.9 kN/m (U = 50 m/s, C_D = 0.8, D = 4 m) on the L = 1,018 m main span. Treating the main span as a beam restrained by the towers with limited lateral stiffness from the stays, an upper bound from a simply supported beam is δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI); with a combined lateral EI of 2.0×10¹⁰ kN·m² for the two boxes and L⁴ = 1,018⁴ ≈ 1.074×10¹², δ = 5×4.9×1.074×10¹²/(384×2.0×10¹⁰) ≈ 2.63×10¹³/7.68×10¹² ≈ 3.4 m. The published wind deflection of about 2.2 m is smaller, implying that the pendulum action of the stays and tower restraint remove about 35% of the lateral movement (1 − 2.2/3.4 ≈ 0.35). At 40 m/s both w and δ scale by (40/50)² = 0.64. EI and coefficients are teaching assumptions, not design values for this bridge.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b009-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁」與「混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck\" and \"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b009-v13-01","title":"颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「中央開槽雙箱梁」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Split twin-box deck” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"昂船洲大橋位於葵青貨櫃碼頭入口，颱風季的強風紊流度高，主跨 1,018 m 的橋面又輕又柔，風力同時造成橫向彎曲、扭轉與可能的顫振。設計者把約 53 m 寬的橋面分成兩個流線形鋼箱梁，中間留空並以橫梁連接：開槽讓上下表面的壓力差得以洩放，提高扭轉顫振的臨界風速，並降低渦流鎖定的振幅。公開設計資料顯示，零攻角無車時顫振臨界風速約 95 m/s，但攻角變為 ±5° 時降到約 50 m/s，說明颱風紊流造成的攻角變化才是控制因素。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「中央開槽雙箱梁」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Stonecutters Bridge sits at the entrance to the Kwai Tsing container terminals, where typhoon winds are highly turbulent, and the 1,018 m main-span deck is light and flexible, so wind causes lateral bending, torsion and potentially flutter. The designers split the roughly 53 m deck into two streamlined steel boxes with an open gap between them, linked by cross girders: the gap vents the pressure difference between upper and lower surfaces, raising the torsional flutter speed and reducing vortex lock-in amplitudes. Published design data show a flutter speed of about 95 m/s at zero incidence without traffic, falling to about 50 m/s at ±5°, so the angle-of-attack changes caused by typhoon turbulence govern. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Split twin-box deck” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：橋面橫向風力 w = ½ρU²·C_D·D。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Lateral wind load on the deck w = ½ρU²·C_D·D.","failure":"常見誤解：「橋面越寬越重，風就越吹不動，所以千米跨只要加重即可抗颱風。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A wider, heavier deck is always harder for wind to move, so a 1 km span only needs more weight to resist typhoons.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「中央開槽雙箱梁」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Split twin-box deck”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-01-k1","title":"颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁","titleEn":"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck","text":"昂船洲大橋位於葵青貨櫃碼頭入口，颱風季的強風紊流度高，主跨 1,018 m 的橋面又輕又柔，風力同時造成橫向彎曲、扭轉與可能的顫振。設計者把約 53 m 寬的橋面分成兩個流線形鋼箱梁，中間留空並以橫梁連接：開槽讓上下表面的壓力差得以洩放，提高扭轉顫振的臨界風速，並降低渦流鎖定的振幅。","textEn":"Stonecutters Bridge sits at the entrance to the Kwai Tsing container terminals, where typhoon winds are highly turbulent, and the 1,018 m main-span deck is light and flexible, so wind causes lateral bending, torsion and potentially flutter. The designers split the roughly 53 m deck into two streamlined steel boxes with an open gap between them, linked by cross girders: the gap vents the pressure difference between upper and lower surfaces, raising the torsional flutter speed and reducing vortex lock-in amplitudes.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：橋面越寬越重，風就越吹不動，所以千米跨只要加重即可抗颱風。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A wider, heavier deck is always harder for wind to move, so a 1 km span only needs more weight to resist typhoons. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck\" is correct?","options":["橋面越寬越重，風就越吹不動，所以千米跨只要加重即可抗颱風。","昂船洲大橋位於葵青貨櫃碼頭入口，颱風季的強風紊流度高，主跨 1,018 m 的橋面又輕又柔，風力同時造成橫向彎曲、扭轉與可能的顫振。","塔梁之間只要用固定支承鎖死，橋就最穩。"],"optionsEn":["A wider, heavier deck is always harder for wind to move, so a 1 km span only needs more weight to resist typhoons.","Stonecutters Bridge sits at the entrance to the Kwai Tsing container terminals, where typhoon winds are highly turbulent, and the 1,018 m main-span deck is light and flexible, so wind causes lateral bending, torsion and potentially flutter.","Fixing the deck rigidly to the tower always makes the bridge most stable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"昂船洲大橋位於葵青貨櫃碼頭入口，颱風季的強風紊流度高，主跨 1,018 m 的橋面又輕又柔，風力同時造成橫向彎曲、扭轉與可能的顫振。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Stonecutters Bridge sits at the entrance to the Kwai Tsing container terminals, where typhoon winds are highly turbulent, and the 1,018 m main-span deck is light and flexible, so wind causes lateral bending, torsion and potentially flutter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b009-v13-02","title":"颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁：定量估算","titleEn":"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「中央開槽雙箱梁」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Split twin-box deck” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：橋面橫向風力 w = ½ρU²·C_D·D。取 ρ = 1.225 kg/m³、U = 50 m/s、C_D = 0.8（以箱高為參考）、D = 4 m：q = 0.5×1.225×50² ≈ 1,531 Pa，w = 1,531×0.8×4 ≈ 4.9 kN/m，作用於 1,018 m 主跨合計約 5.0 MN；風速降為 40 m/s 時 w ≈ 3.1 kN/m，與 U² 成正比。係數與箱高為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Lateral wind load on the deck w = ½ρU²·C_D·D. With ρ = 1.225 kg/m³, U = 50 m/s, C_D = 0.8 referenced to box depth and D = 4 m, q = 0.5×1.225×50² ≈ 1,531 Pa and w = 1,531×0.8×4 ≈ 4.9 kN/m, about 5.0 MN over the 1,018 m main span; at 40 m/s w ≈ 3.1 kN/m, scaling with U². Coefficient and depth are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以風洞斷面模型量測不同攻角下的阻力、升力與扭矩係數，並做顫振導數識別；把颱風紊流的攻角分布代入顫振分析，確認在最不利攻角下的臨界風速仍高於設計要求，再以全橋分析計算跨中側向撓度與塔底彎矩。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure drag, lift and moment coefficients at several angles of attack on section models and identify flutter derivatives; feed the typhoon turbulence distribution of incidence into the flutter analysis to confirm that the critical speed at the worst angle still exceeds the requirement, then compute mid-span lateral deflection and tower-base moments globally.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"橋面橫向風力 w = ½ρU²·C_D·D。取 ρ = 1.225 kg/m³、U = 50 m/s、C_D = 0.8（以箱高為參考）、D = 4 m：q = 0.5×1.225×50² ≈ 1,531 Pa，w = 1,531×0.8×4 ≈ 4.9 kN/m，作用於 1,018 m 主跨合計約 5.0 MN；風速降為 40 m/s 時 w ≈ 3.1 kN/m，與 U² 成正比。係數與箱高為教學假設。","textEn":"Lateral wind load on the deck w = ½ρU²·C_D·D. With ρ = 1.225 kg/m³, U = 50 m/s, C_D = 0.8 referenced to box depth and D = 4 m, q = 0.5×1.225×50² ≈ 1,531 Pa and w = 1,531×0.8×4 ≈ 4.9 kN/m, about 5.0 MN over the 1,018 m main span; at 40 m/s w ≈ 3.1 kN/m, scaling with U². Coefficient and depth are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck\", which statement holds?","options":["同一座橋的斜拉索應該都一樣粗，才方便施工和維護。","鋼梁與混凝土梁只要用螺栓頭對頭接上，力量就會平均傳遞。","橋面橫向風力 w = ½ρU²·C_D·D。"],"optionsEn":["All stays on one bridge should have the same size for easier construction and maintenance.","Bolting the steel girder end to the concrete girder end transfers force evenly.","Lateral wind load on the deck w = ½ρU²·C_D·D."],"answer":2,"explanation":"橋面橫向風力 w = ½ρU²·C_D·D。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Lateral wind load on the deck w = ½ρU²·C_D·D. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b009-v13-03","title":"颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「中央開槽雙箱梁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Split twin-box deck” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以風洞斷面模型量測不同攻角下的阻力、升力與扭矩係數，並做顫振導數識別；把颱風紊流的攻角分布代入顫振分析，確認在最不利攻角下的臨界風速仍高於設計要求，再以全橋分析計算跨中側向撓度與塔底彎矩。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure drag, lift and moment coefficients at several angles of attack on section models and identify flutter derivatives; feed the typhoon turbulence distribution of incidence into the flutter analysis to confirm that the critical speed at the worst angle still exceeds the requirement, then compute mid-span lateral deflection and tower-base moments globally. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：風工程報告應明列各攻角的顫振臨界風速、有無交通的差異與試驗模型所含的附屬物；任何欄杆、防撞護欄或檢修軌道的形狀變更都要回到風工程顧問複核。","observationEn":"Site practice: The wind report should tabulate flutter speeds by angle of attack, with and without traffic, and list the attachments modelled; any change to railings, barriers or inspection rails goes back to the wind consultant for review.","failure":"注意干擾：若只以零攻角的試驗結果判定顫振安全，強紊流下的實際攻角可能使臨界風速降低近一半；開槽寬度或橫梁形狀在細部設計中被修改而未重新試驗，也可能出現未預期的渦振或扭轉不穩定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Judging flutter safety only from zero-incidence results can overlook that real angles of attack in strong turbulence nearly halve the critical speed; altering the gap width or cross-girder shape in detailed design without retesting can introduce unexpected vortex vibration or torsional instability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以風洞斷面模型量測不同攻角下的阻力、升力與扭矩係數，並做顫振導數識別；把颱風紊流的攻角分布代入顫振分析，確認在最不利攻角下的臨界風速仍高於設計要求，再以全橋分析計算跨中側向撓度與塔底彎矩。","textEn":"Measure drag, lift and moment coefficients at several angles of attack on section models and identify flutter derivatives; feed the typhoon turbulence distribution of incidence into the flutter analysis to confirm that the critical speed at the worst angle still exceeds the requirement, then compute mid-span lateral deflection and tower-base moments globally.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"風工程報告應明列各攻角的顫振臨界風速、有無交通的差異與試驗模型所含的附屬物；任何欄杆、防撞護欄或檢修軌道的形狀變更都要回到風工程顧問複核。","textEn":"The wind report should tabulate flutter speeds by angle of attack, with and without traffic, and list the attachments modelled; any change to railings, barriers or inspection rails goes back to the wind consultant for review.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck\"?","options":["以風洞斷面模型量測不同攻角下的阻力、升力與扭矩係數，並做顫振導數識別。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","大橋跨中撓度達到一兩公尺，就表示結構不安全。"],"optionsEn":["Measure drag, lift and moment coefficients at several angles of attack on section models and identify flutter derivatives.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A mid-span deflection of one or two metres means the bridge is unsafe."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以風洞斷面模型量測不同攻角下的阻力、升力與扭矩係數，並做顫振導數識別；把颱風紊流的攻角分布代入顫振分析，確認在最不利攻角下的臨界風速仍高於設計要求，再以全橋分析計算跨中側向撓度與塔底彎矩。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure drag, lift and moment coefficients at several angles of attack on section models and identify flutter derivatives; feed the typhoon turbulence distribution of incidence into the flutter analysis to confirm that the critical speed at the worst angle still exceeds the requirement, then compute mid-span lateral deflection and tower-base moments globally. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b009-v13-04","title":"颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁：失效診斷","titleEn":"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「中央開槽雙箱梁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Split twin-box deck” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只以零攻角的試驗結果判定顫振安全，強紊流下的實際攻角可能使臨界風速降低近一半；開槽寬度或橫梁形狀在細部設計中被修改而未重新試驗，也可能出現未預期的渦振或扭轉不穩定。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Judging flutter safety only from zero-incidence results can overlook that real angles of attack in strong turbulence nearly halve the critical speed; altering the gap width or cross-girder shape in detailed design without retesting can introduce unexpected vortex vibration or torsional instability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：公開設計資料顯示，零攻角無車時顫振臨界風速約 95 m/s，但攻角變為 ±5° 時降到約 50 m/s，說明颱風紊流造成的攻角變化才是控制因素。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Published design data show a flutter speed of about 95 m/s at zero incidence without traffic, falling to about 50 m/s at ±5°, so the angle-of-attack changes caused by typhoon turbulence govern.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「橋面越寬越重，風就越吹不動，所以千米跨只要加重即可抗颱風。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A wider, heavier deck is always harder for wind to move, so a 1 km span only needs more weight to resist typhoons.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只以零攻角的試驗結果判定顫振安全，強紊流下的實際攻角可能使臨界風速降低近一半；開槽寬度或橫梁形狀在細部設計中被修改而未重新試驗，也可能出現未預期的渦振或扭轉不穩定。","textEn":"Judging flutter safety only from zero-incidence results can overlook that real angles of attack in strong turbulence nearly halve the critical speed; altering the gap width or cross-girder shape in detailed design without retesting can introduce unexpected vortex vibration or torsional instability.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「颱風風荷載與分離式雙箱梁」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Typhoon wind load and the split twin-box deck\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只以零攻角的試驗結果判定顫振安全，強紊流下的實際攻角可能使臨界風速降低近一半。","塔梁之間只要用固定支承鎖死，橋就最穩。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Judging flutter safety only from zero-incidence results can overlook that real angles of attack in strong turbulence nearly halve the critical speed.","Fixing the deck rigidly to the tower always makes the bridge most stable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只以零攻角的試驗結果判定顫振安全，強紊流下的實際攻角可能使臨界風速降低近一半；開槽寬度或橫梁形狀在細部設計中被修改而未重新試驗，也可能出現未預期的渦振或扭轉不穩定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Judging flutter safety only from zero-incidence results can overlook that real angles of attack in strong turbulence nearly halve the critical speed; altering the gap width or cross-girder shape in detailed design without retesting can introduce unexpected vortex vibration or torsional instability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b009-v13-05","title":"混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「塔–梁液壓緩衝器」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tower–deck hydraulic buffers” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"昂船洲大橋兩側背跨各長 289 m，由 79.75、70、70、69.25 m 四跨預力混凝土雙箱梁組成，混凝土的重量提供平衡主跨鋼梁的壓重，密布的背跨橋墩則讓背索錨固點接近固定，提高整體勁度。主跨與背跨連成連續橋面，溫度造成的伸縮必須能自由發生；但颱風陣風、地震與煞車屬於快速荷載，橋面不能任意滑動。因此塔與梁之間在橋面高程設置液壓緩衝器：慢速溫度位移時油可通過孔道，幾乎不產生力；快速荷載時閥門鎖住，緩衝器像剛性連桿把縱向力傳給橋塔。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「塔–梁液壓緩衝器」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each back span of Stonecutters Bridge is 289 m long, made of four prestressed concrete twin-box spans of 79.75, 70, 70 and 69.25 m; the concrete weight ballasts the steel main span, and the closely spaced back-span piers make the back-stay anchor points nearly fixed, raising global stiffness. The main and back spans form a continuous deck whose thermal expansion must occur freely, but typhoon gusts, earthquakes and braking are fast loads under which the deck must not slide. Hydraulic buffers between tower and deck at deck level therefore let oil pass through orifices during slow thermal movement, producing almost no force, and lock under fast loads so the buffer acts as a rigid link carrying longitudinal force to the tower. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Tower–deck hydraulic buffers” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT，取 α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C、L = 560 m、ΔT = 40 °C：ΔL ≈ 0.269 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT; with α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C, L = 560 m and ΔT = 40 °C, ΔL ≈ 0.269 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「塔梁之間只要用固定支承鎖死，橋就最穩。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Fixing the deck rigidly to the tower always makes the bridge most stable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「塔–梁液壓緩衝器」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Tower–deck hydraulic buffers”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-05-k1","title":"混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接","titleEn":"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection","text":"昂船洲大橋兩側背跨各長 289 m，由 79.75、70、70、69.25 m 四跨預力混凝土雙箱梁組成，混凝土的重量提供平衡主跨鋼梁的壓重，密布的背跨橋墩則讓背索錨固點接近固定，提高整體勁度。主跨與背跨連成連續橋面，溫度造成的伸縮必須能自由發生；但颱風陣風、地震與煞車屬於快速荷載，橋面不能任意滑動。","textEn":"Each back span of Stonecutters Bridge is 289 m long, made of four prestressed concrete twin-box spans of 79.75, 70, 70 and 69.25 m; the concrete weight ballasts the steel main span, and the closely spaced back-span piers make the back-stay anchor points nearly fixed, raising global stiffness. The main and back spans form a continuous deck whose thermal expansion must occur freely, but typhoon gusts, earthquakes and braking are fast loads under which the deck must not slide.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：塔梁之間只要用固定支承鎖死，橋就最穩。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Fixing the deck rigidly to the tower always makes the bridge most stable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection\" is correct?","options":["塔梁之間只要用固定支承鎖死，橋就最穩。","不鏽鋼外皮只是為了外觀好看，不參與結構受力。","昂船洲大橋兩側背跨各長 289 m，由 79.75、70、70、69.25 m 四跨預力混凝土雙箱梁組成，混凝土的重量提供平衡主跨鋼梁的壓重，密布的背跨橋墩則讓背索錨固點接近固定，提高整體勁度。"],"optionsEn":["Fixing the deck rigidly to the tower always makes the bridge most stable.","The stainless skin is only for appearance and carries no structural load.","Each back span of Stonecutters Bridge is 289 m long, made of four prestressed concrete twin-box spans of 79.75, 70, 70 and 69.25 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"昂船洲大橋兩側背跨各長 289 m，由 79.75、70、70、69.25 m 四跨預力混凝土雙箱梁組成，混凝土的重量提供平衡主跨鋼梁的壓重，密布的背跨橋墩則讓背索錨固點接近固定，提高整體勁度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each back span of Stonecutters Bridge is 289 m long, made of four prestressed concrete twin-box spans of 79.75, 70, 70 and 69.25 m; the concrete weight ballasts the steel main span, and the closely spaced back-span piers make the back-stay anchor points nearly fixed, raising global stiffness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b009-v13-06","title":"混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接：定量估算","titleEn":"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塔–梁液壓緩衝器」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tower–deck hydraulic buffers” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT，取 α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C、L = 560 m、ΔT = 40 °C：ΔL ≈ 0.269 m。若這 40 °C 在 6 小時內發生，平均速度 0.269/21,600 ≈ 1.2×10⁻⁵ m/s，遠低於陣風下橋面約 0.1 m/s 的擺動速度，緩衝器可據此區分兩種荷載。背跨與主跨長度比 289/1,018 ≈ 0.28。L 與 ΔT 為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT; with α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C, L = 560 m and ΔT = 40 °C, ΔL ≈ 0.269 m. If the 40 °C change occurs over 6 hours, the mean velocity is 0.269/21,600 ≈ 1.2×10⁻⁵ m/s, far below the roughly 0.1 m/s deck motion in gusts, so the buffer can distinguish the two. The back-to-main span ratio is 289/1,018 ≈ 0.28. L and ΔT are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：緩衝器出廠以低速蠕動試驗確認溫度位移下的阻力上限，以高速試驗確認鎖定力與鎖定位移；安裝後量測不同季節的塔梁相對位移與溫度回歸，並在颱風事件後檢視紀錄，確認鎖定行為與設計一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Factory-test the buffers at creep speeds to confirm the resistance limit under thermal movement, and at high speed to confirm lock-up force and lock-up displacement; after installation regress tower–deck relative displacement against temperature across seasons and review records after each typhoon to confirm lock-up as designed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT，取 α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C、L = 560 m、ΔT = 40 °C：ΔL ≈ 0.269 m。若這 40 °C 在 6 小時內發生，平均速度 0.269/21,600 ≈ 1.2×10⁻⁵ m/s，遠低於陣風下橋面約 0.1 m/s 的擺動速度，緩衝器可據此區分兩種荷載。背跨與主跨長度比 289/1,018 ≈ 0.28。L 與 ΔT 為教學假設。","textEn":"Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT; with α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C, L = 560 m and ΔT = 40 °C, ΔL ≈ 0.269 m. If the 40 °C change occurs over 6 hours, the mean velocity is 0.269/21,600 ≈ 1.2×10⁻⁵ m/s, far below the roughly 0.1 m/s deck motion in gusts, so the buffer can distinguish the two. The back-to-main span ratio is 289/1,018 ≈ 0.28. L and ΔT are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection\", which statement holds?","options":["溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT，取 α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C、L = 560 m、ΔT = 40 °C：ΔL ≈ 0.269 m。","成橋狀態能抗颱風，施工中的懸臂狀態自然也能。","風洞模型只要幾何縮尺正確，試驗結果就能直接放大套用到實橋。"],"optionsEn":["Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT; with α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C, L = 560 m and ΔT = 40 °C, ΔL ≈ 0.269 m.","If the completed bridge resists typhoons, the cantilever stage naturally does too.","If a wind-tunnel model is geometrically correct, its results scale directly to the full bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT，取 α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C、L = 560 m、ΔT = 40 °C：ΔL ≈ 0.269 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT; with α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C, L = 560 m and ΔT = 40 °C, ΔL ≈ 0.269 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b009-v13-07","title":"混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塔–梁液壓緩衝器」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tower–deck hydraulic buffers” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"緩衝器出廠以低速蠕動試驗確認溫度位移下的阻力上限，以高速試驗確認鎖定力與鎖定位移；安裝後量測不同季節的塔梁相對位移與溫度回歸，並在颱風事件後檢視紀錄，確認鎖定行為與設計一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Factory-test the buffers at creep speeds to confirm the resistance limit under thermal movement, and at high speed to confirm lock-up force and lock-up displacement; after installation regress tower–deck relative displacement against temperature across seasons and review records after each typhoon to confirm lock-up as designed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：維護手冊應規定緩衝器的檢查頻率、漏油判定、行程刻度讀數與颱風後的專項檢查；更換緩衝器時須有臨時縱向約束方案與交通管制。","observationEn":"Site practice: The maintenance manual should set buffer inspection frequency, leak criteria, stroke-scale readings and post-typhoon special checks; buffer replacement needs a temporary longitudinal restraint scheme and traffic management.","failure":"注意干擾：若緩衝器密封漏油或閥門卡滯，可能在溫度變化時產生不應有的大力，使塔或支承受額外彎矩；反之若鎖定失效，颱風陣風使橋面縱向往復移動，加速伸縮縫與支承磨耗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Leaking seals or a stuck valve can generate large unintended forces during temperature change, adding moment to the tower or bearings; conversely, failed lock-up lets typhoon gusts shuttle the deck longitudinally, accelerating joint and bearing wear. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"緩衝器出廠以低速蠕動試驗確認溫度位移下的阻力上限，以高速試驗確認鎖定力與鎖定位移；安裝後量測不同季節的塔梁相對位移與溫度回歸，並在颱風事件後檢視紀錄，確認鎖定行為與設計一致。","textEn":"Factory-test the buffers at creep speeds to confirm the resistance limit under thermal movement, and at high speed to confirm lock-up force and lock-up displacement; after installation regress tower–deck relative displacement against temperature across seasons and review records after each typhoon to confirm lock-up as designed.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"維護手冊應規定緩衝器的檢查頻率、漏油判定、行程刻度讀數與颱風後的專項檢查；更換緩衝器時須有臨時縱向約束方案與交通管制。","textEn":"The maintenance manual should set buffer inspection frequency, leak criteria, stroke-scale readings and post-typhoon special checks; buffer replacement needs a temporary longitudinal restraint scheme and traffic management.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","緩衝器出廠以低速蠕動試驗確認溫度位移下的阻力上限，以高速試驗確認鎖定力與鎖定位移。","只要混凝土強度高，海水環境下就不會有鋼筋腐蝕問題。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Factory-test the buffers at creep speeds to confirm the resistance limit under thermal movement, and at high speed to confirm lock-up force and lock-up displacement.","High-strength concrete alone prevents reinforcement corrosion in seawater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"緩衝器出廠以低速蠕動試驗確認溫度位移下的阻力上限，以高速試驗確認鎖定力與鎖定位移；安裝後量測不同季節的塔梁相對位移與溫度回歸，並在颱風事件後檢視紀錄，確認鎖定行為與設計一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Factory-test the buffers at creep speeds to confirm the resistance limit under thermal movement, and at high speed to confirm lock-up force and lock-up displacement; after installation regress tower–deck relative displacement against temperature across seasons and review records after each typhoon to confirm lock-up as designed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b009-v13-08","title":"混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塔–梁液壓緩衝器」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tower–deck hydraulic buffers” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若緩衝器密封漏油或閥門卡滯，可能在溫度變化時產生不應有的大力，使塔或支承受額外彎矩；反之若鎖定失效，颱風陣風使橋面縱向往復移動，加速伸縮縫與支承磨耗。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Leaking seals or a stuck valve can generate large unintended forces during temperature change, adding moment to the tower or bearings; conversely, failed lock-up lets typhoon gusts shuttle the deck longitudinally, accelerating joint and bearing wear. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此塔與梁之間在橋面高程設置液壓緩衝器：慢速溫度位移時油可通過孔道，幾乎不產生力；快速荷載時閥門鎖住，緩衝器像剛性連桿把縱向力傳給橋塔。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Hydraulic buffers between tower and deck at deck level therefore let oil pass through orifices during slow thermal movement, producing almost no force, and lock under fast loads so the buffer acts as a rigid link carrying longitudinal force to the tower.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「塔梁之間只要用固定支承鎖死，橋就最穩。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Fixing the deck rigidly to the tower always makes the bridge most stable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若緩衝器密封漏油或閥門卡滯，可能在溫度變化時產生不應有的大力，使塔或支承受額外彎矩；反之若鎖定失效，颱風陣風使橋面縱向往復移動，加速伸縮縫與支承磨耗。","textEn":"Leaking seals or a stuck valve can generate large unintended forces during temperature change, adding moment to the tower or bearings; conversely, failed lock-up lets typhoon gusts shuttle the deck longitudinally, accelerating joint and bearing wear.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「混凝土背跨壓重與塔梁縱向連接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Concrete back-span ballast and the tower–deck connection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","不鏽鋼外皮只是為了外觀好看，不參與結構受力。","若緩衝器密封漏油或閥門卡滯，可能在溫度變化時產生不應有的大力，使塔或支承受額外彎矩；反之若鎖定失效，颱風陣風使橋面縱向往復移動，加速伸縮縫與支承磨耗。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The stainless skin is only for appearance and carries no structural load.","Leaking seals or a stuck valve can generate large unintended forces during temperature change, adding moment to the tower or bearings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若緩衝器密封漏油或閥門卡滯，可能在溫度變化時產生不應有的大力，使塔或支承受額外彎矩；反之若鎖定失效，颱風陣風使橋面縱向往復移動，加速伸縮縫與支承磨耗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Leaking seals or a stuck valve can generate large unintended forces during temperature change, adding moment to the tower or bearings; conversely, failed lock-up lets typhoon gusts shuttle the deck longitudinally, accelerating joint and bearing wear. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b009-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面」與「224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section\" and \"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b009-v13-09","title":"不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「雙相不鏽鋼外皮」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duplex stainless skin” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"昂船洲大橋的塔為中空單柱，斷面由下方的橢圓形逐漸收成上方的圓形，塔頂達主水平基準以上約 298 m。約 +175 m 以下為鋼筋混凝土，以上改為鋼—混凝土複合段，外層是雙相不鏽鋼板，不只是飾面，而是與內部混凝土共同受力的結構元件。斜索錨固集中在上塔，需要高勁度與高強度；不鏽鋼外皮同時省去日後高空重新塗裝，降低維護成本與風險。複合段設計重點在剪力釘或連接件把鋼皮與混凝土結合，避免溫差與乾縮使兩者分離。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「雙相不鏽鋼外皮」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Stonecutters towers are hollow monopoles whose section tapers from an ellipse below to a circle above, reaching about +298 mPD. Below about +175 m they are reinforced concrete; above, a steel–concrete composite section with a duplex stainless steel outer skin that is a structural element acting with the concrete, not cladding. Stay anchorages concentrate in the upper tower and need high stiffness and strength, and the stainless skin avoids repainting at height, reducing maintenance cost and risk. The composite design hinges on studs or connectors that bond skin and concrete so temperature differences and shrinkage do not separate them. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Duplex stainless skin” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：換算斷面軸向勁度 EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Transformed axial stiffness EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s.","failure":"常見誤解：「不鏽鋼外皮只是為了外觀好看，不參與結構受力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The stainless skin is only for appearance and carries no structural load.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「雙相不鏽鋼外皮」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Duplex stainless skin”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-09-k1","title":"不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面","titleEn":"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section","text":"昂船洲大橋的塔為中空單柱，斷面由下方的橢圓形逐漸收成上方的圓形，塔頂達主水平基準以上約 298 m。約 +175 m 以下為鋼筋混凝土，以上改為鋼—混凝土複合段，外層是雙相不鏽鋼板，不只是飾面，而是與內部混凝土共同受力的結構元件。","textEn":"The Stonecutters towers are hollow monopoles whose section tapers from an ellipse below to a circle above, reaching about +298 mPD. Below about +175 m they are reinforced concrete; above, a steel–concrete composite section with a duplex stainless steel outer skin that is a structural element acting with the concrete, not cladding.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：不鏽鋼外皮只是為了外觀好看，不參與結構受力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The stainless skin is only for appearance and carries no structural load. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section\" is correct?","options":["昂船洲大橋的塔為中空單柱，斷面由下方的橢圓形逐漸收成上方的圓形，塔頂達主水平基準以上約 298 m。","不鏽鋼外皮只是為了外觀好看，不參與結構受力。","同一座橋的斜拉索應該都一樣粗，才方便施工和維護。"],"optionsEn":["The Stonecutters towers are hollow monopoles whose section tapers from an ellipse below to a circle above, reaching about +298 mPD.","The stainless skin is only for appearance and carries no structural load.","All stays on one bridge should have the same size for easier construction and maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"昂船洲大橋的塔為中空單柱，斷面由下方的橢圓形逐漸收成上方的圓形，塔頂達主水平基準以上約 298 m。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Stonecutters towers are hollow monopoles whose section tapers from an ellipse below to a circle above, reaching about +298 mPD. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b009-v13-10","title":"不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面：定量估算","titleEn":"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙相不鏽鋼外皮」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duplex stainless skin” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：換算斷面軸向勁度 EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s。取周長 30 m、外皮 20 mm，A_s = 0.6 m²；混凝土 A_c = 18 m²，E_c = 40 GPa、E_s = 200 GPa：E_c·A_c = 720 GN，E_s·A_s = 120 GN，外皮貢獻 120/840 ≈ 14% 的軸向勁度。尺寸為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Transformed axial stiffness EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s. With a 30 m perimeter and 20 mm skin, A_s = 0.6 m²; with A_c = 18 m², E_c = 40 GPa and E_s = 200 GPa, E_c·A_c = 720 GN and E_s·A_s = 120 GN, so the skin supplies 120/840 ≈ 14% of the axial stiffness. Dimensions are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：鋼皮分段在工廠製作時量測真圓度與焊接變形，現場吊裝後以測量確認軸線；剪力連接件做抽樣拉拔或彎曲試驗，混凝土灌注後以敲擊或超音波檢查鋼皮與混凝土是否脫空。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure roundness and weld distortion of skin segments in the shop and survey the axis after erection; proof-test sample shear connectors by pull-out or bend tests, and after concreting check for voids between skin and concrete by tapping or ultrasonic testing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"換算斷面軸向勁度 EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s。取周長 30 m、外皮 20 mm，A_s = 0.6 m²；混凝土 A_c = 18 m²，E_c = 40 GPa、E_s = 200 GPa：E_c·A_c = 720 GN，E_s·A_s = 120 GN，外皮貢獻 120/840 ≈ 14% 的軸向勁度。尺寸為教學假設。","textEn":"Transformed axial stiffness EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s. With a 30 m perimeter and 20 mm skin, A_s = 0.6 m²; with A_c = 18 m², E_c = 40 GPa and E_s = 200 GPa, E_c·A_c = 720 GN and E_s·A_s = 120 GN, so the skin supplies 120/840 ≈ 14% of the axial stiffness. Dimensions are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼梁與混凝土梁只要用螺栓頭對頭接上，力量就會平均傳遞。","換算斷面軸向勁度 EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s。","大橋跨中撓度達到一兩公尺，就表示結構不安全。"],"optionsEn":["Bolting the steel girder end to the concrete girder end transfers force evenly.","Transformed axial stiffness EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s.","A mid-span deflection of one or two metres means the bridge is unsafe."],"answer":1,"explanation":"換算斷面軸向勁度 EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Transformed axial stiffness EA = E_c·A_c + E_s·A_s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b009-v13-11","title":"不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙相不鏽鋼外皮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duplex stainless skin” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"鋼皮分段在工廠製作時量測真圓度與焊接變形，現場吊裝後以測量確認軸線；剪力連接件做抽樣拉拔或彎曲試驗，混凝土灌注後以敲擊或超音波檢查鋼皮與混凝土是否脫空。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure roundness and weld distortion of skin segments in the shop and survey the axis after erection; proof-test sample shear connectors by pull-out or bend tests, and after concreting check for voids between skin and concrete by tapping or ultrasonic testing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：複合塔段的施工計畫要規定每節鋼皮的定位公差、混凝土分層澆置高度與側壓限制，以及脫空檢測的抽樣比例；不同金屬接觸點的絕緣細部須在圖上標示。","observationEn":"Site practice: The composite-tower method statement should set positioning tolerances for each skin segment, concrete lift heights and lateral-pressure limits, and the sampling rate for void detection; insulation details at dissimilar-metal contacts must be shown on the drawings.","failure":"注意干擾：若鋼皮與混凝土間灌漿不密實或連接件不足，鋼皮在日照溫差下局部鼓起，複合作用消失，錨固區的應力集中提高；不同金屬接觸處若未隔離，也可能出現電化學腐蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incomplete concrete fill or too few connectors lets the skin bulge locally under solar temperature differences, losing composite action and raising stress concentrations in the anchorage zone; contact between dissimilar metals without isolation can also cause galvanic corrosion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"鋼皮分段在工廠製作時量測真圓度與焊接變形，現場吊裝後以測量確認軸線；剪力連接件做抽樣拉拔或彎曲試驗，混凝土灌注後以敲擊或超音波檢查鋼皮與混凝土是否脫空。","textEn":"Measure roundness and weld distortion of skin segments in the shop and survey the axis after erection; proof-test sample shear connectors by pull-out or bend tests, and after concreting check for voids between skin and concrete by tapping or ultrasonic testing.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"複合塔段的施工計畫要規定每節鋼皮的定位公差、混凝土分層澆置高度與側壓限制，以及脫空檢測的抽樣比例；不同金屬接觸點的絕緣細部須在圖上標示。","textEn":"The composite-tower method statement should set positioning tolerances for each skin segment, concrete lift heights and lateral-pressure limits, and the sampling rate for void detection; insulation details at dissimilar-metal contacts must be shown on the drawings.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","斜拉索索力一旦施工完成就不會再改變，不需要追蹤。","鋼皮分段在工廠製作時量測真圓度與焊接變形，現場吊裝後以測量確認軸線；剪力連接件做抽樣拉拔或彎曲試驗，混凝土灌注後以敲擊或超音波檢查鋼皮與混凝土是否脫空。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Stay forces never change after construction, so they need no tracking.","Measure roundness and weld distortion of skin segments in the shop and survey the axis after erection."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋼皮分段在工廠製作時量測真圓度與焊接變形，現場吊裝後以測量確認軸線；剪力連接件做抽樣拉拔或彎曲試驗，混凝土灌注後以敲擊或超音波檢查鋼皮與混凝土是否脫空。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure roundness and weld distortion of skin segments in the shop and survey the axis after erection; proof-test sample shear connectors by pull-out or bend tests, and after concreting check for voids between skin and concrete by tapping or ultrasonic testing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b009-v13-12","title":"不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙相不鏽鋼外皮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duplex stainless skin” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若鋼皮與混凝土間灌漿不密實或連接件不足，鋼皮在日照溫差下局部鼓起，複合作用消失，錨固區的應力集中提高；不同金屬接觸處若未隔離，也可能出現電化學腐蝕。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incomplete concrete fill or too few connectors lets the skin bulge locally under solar temperature differences, losing composite action and raising stress concentrations in the anchorage zone; contact between dissimilar metals without isolation can also cause galvanic corrosion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：複合段設計重點在剪力釘或連接件把鋼皮與混凝土結合，避免溫差與乾縮使兩者分離。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The composite design hinges on studs or connectors that bond skin and concrete so temperature differences and shrinkage do not separate them.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「不鏽鋼外皮只是為了外觀好看，不參與結構受力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The stainless skin is only for appearance and carries no structural load.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若鋼皮與混凝土間灌漿不密實或連接件不足，鋼皮在日照溫差下局部鼓起，複合作用消失，錨固區的應力集中提高；不同金屬接觸處若未隔離，也可能出現電化學腐蝕。","textEn":"Incomplete concrete fill or too few connectors lets the skin bulge locally under solar temperature differences, losing composite action and raising stress concentrations in the anchorage zone; contact between dissimilar metals without isolation can also cause galvanic corrosion.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「不鏽鋼複合上塔與單柱塔斷面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Composite stainless upper tower and monopole section\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若鋼皮與混凝土間灌漿不密實或連接件不足，鋼皮在日照溫差下局部鼓起，複合作用消失，錨固區的應力集中提高；不同金屬接觸處若未隔離，也可能出現電化學腐蝕。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","同一座橋的斜拉索應該都一樣粗，才方便施工和維護。"],"optionsEn":["Incomplete concrete fill or too few connectors lets the skin bulge locally under solar temperature differences, losing composite action and raising stress concentrations in the anchorage zone.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All stays on one bridge should have the same size for easier construction and maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若鋼皮與混凝土間灌漿不密實或連接件不足，鋼皮在日照溫差下局部鼓起，複合作用消失，錨固區的應力集中提高；不同金屬接觸處若未隔離，也可能出現電化學腐蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incomplete concrete fill or too few connectors lets the skin bulge locally under solar temperature differences, losing composite action and raising stress concentrations in the anchorage zone; contact between dissimilar metals without isolation can also cause galvanic corrosion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b009-v13-13","title":"224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「塔內錨箱」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tower anchor boxes” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"全橋 224 根斜拉索以雙索面修正扇形配置，主跨錨距約 18 m、背跨約 10 m，最長約 540 m、單根約 70 t，全部斜索合計約 7,200 t。公開設計資料顯示索的外徑由塔附近的 113 mm（163 根鋼線）增到背跨端的 192 mm（499 根鋼線），因為越靠背跨端的背索要平衡越多主跨重量。上塔內約 1,200 t 的鋼錨箱把各索的集中力分散到塔壁，同時讓張拉設備有作業空間。索徑與鋼線數的變化正好反映了扇形配置下索力的分布。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「塔內錨箱」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The bridge has 224 stays in two planes in a modified fan, anchored at about 18 m spacing in the main span and about 10 m in the back spans; the longest is about 540 m and about 70 t, and all stays total about 7,200 t. Published design data show outside diameters rising from 113 mm (163 wires) near the towers to 192 mm (499 wires) toward the back-span ends, because the back stays nearest the ends balance the most main-span weight. Steel anchor boxes of about 1,200 t in the upper towers spread each concentrated stay force into the tower walls and give room for stressing equipment. The change of diameter and wire count mirrors the force distribution in a fan arrangement. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Tower anchor boxes” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：假設鋼線直徑 7 mm、抗拉強度 1,770 MPa：499 根 A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm²，破斷力約 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN，0.45 倍約 15,300 kN；163 根 A ≈ 6,270 mm²，破斷力約 11,100 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assuming 7 mm wires of 1,770 MPa: 499 wires give A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm² and a breaking force of about 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN, with 0.45 of that about 15,300 kN; 163 wires give A ≈ 6,270 mm² and about 11,100 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一座橋的斜拉索應該都一樣粗，才方便施工和維護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All stays on one bridge should have the same size for easier construction and maintenance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「塔內錨箱」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Tower anchor boxes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-13-k1","title":"224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置","titleEn":"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes","text":"全橋 224 根斜拉索以雙索面修正扇形配置，主跨錨距約 18 m、背跨約 10 m，最長約 540 m、單根約 70 t，全部斜索合計約 7,200 t。公開設計資料顯示索的外徑由塔附近的 113 mm（163 根鋼線）增到背跨端的 192 mm（499 根鋼線），因為越靠背跨端的背索要平衡越多主跨重量。","textEn":"The bridge has 224 stays in two planes in a modified fan, anchored at about 18 m spacing in the main span and about 10 m in the back spans; the longest is about 540 m and about 70 t, and all stays total about 7,200 t. Published design data show outside diameters rising from 113 mm (163 wires) near the towers to 192 mm (499 wires) toward the back-span ends, because the back stays nearest the ends balance the most main-span weight.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一座橋的斜拉索應該都一樣粗，才方便施工和維護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All stays on one bridge should have the same size for easier construction and maintenance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes\" is correct?","options":["同一座橋的斜拉索應該都一樣粗，才方便施工和維護。","全橋 224 根斜拉索以雙索面修正扇形配置，主跨錨距約 18 m、背跨約 10 m，最長約 540 m、單根約 70 t，全部斜索合計約 7,200 t。","成橋狀態能抗颱風，施工中的懸臂狀態自然也能。"],"optionsEn":["All stays on one bridge should have the same size for easier construction and maintenance.","The bridge has 224 stays in two planes in a modified fan, anchored at about 18 m spacing in the main span and about 10 m in the back spans.","If the completed bridge resists typhoons, the cantilever stage naturally does too."],"answer":1,"explanation":"全橋 224 根斜拉索以雙索面修正扇形配置，主跨錨距約 18 m、背跨約 10 m，最長約 540 m、單根約 70 t，全部斜索合計約 7,200 t。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The bridge has 224 stays in two planes in a modified fan, anchored at about 18 m spacing in the main span and about 10 m in the back spans; the longest is about 540 m and about 70 t, and all stays total about 7,200 t. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b009-v13-14","title":"224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置：定量估算","titleEn":"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塔內錨箱」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tower anchor boxes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：假設鋼線直徑 7 mm、抗拉強度 1,770 MPa：499 根 A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm²，破斷力約 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN，0.45 倍約 15,300 kN；163 根 A ≈ 6,270 mm²，破斷力約 11,100 kN。最長索 70 t/540 m ≈ 130 kg/m。鋼線直徑與強度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assuming 7 mm wires of 1,770 MPa: 499 wires give A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm² and a breaking force of about 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN, with 0.45 of that about 15,300 kN; 163 wires give A ≈ 6,270 mm² and about 11,100 kN. The longest stay averages 70 t/540 m ≈ 130 kg/m. Wire size and strength are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：斜索與錨具依斜索規範做組裝體疲勞、破斷與防水試驗，並在 1:1 索段做風雨振試驗；錨箱焊道以超音波檢測，安裝後量測每根索的最終力與錨頭位置，與設計表逐一比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test stay and anchorage assemblies for fatigue, ultimate strength and watertightness under stay-cable recommendations, and test full-scale cable sections for wind and rain vibration; inspect anchor-box welds ultrasonically and after installation compare each stay’s final force and anchor-head position with the design table.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"假設鋼線直徑 7 mm、抗拉強度 1,770 MPa：499 根 A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm²，破斷力約 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN，0.45 倍約 15,300 kN；163 根 A ≈ 6,270 mm²，破斷力約 11,100 kN。最長索 70 t/540 m ≈ 130 kg/m。鋼線直徑與強度為教學假設。","textEn":"Assuming 7 mm wires of 1,770 MPa: 499 wires give A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm² and a breaking force of about 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN, with 0.45 of that about 15,300 kN; 163 wires give A ≈ 6,270 mm² and about 11,100 kN. The longest stay averages 70 t/540 m ≈ 130 kg/m. Wire size and strength are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes\", which statement holds?","options":["風洞模型只要幾何縮尺正確，試驗結果就能直接放大套用到實橋。","只要混凝土強度高，海水環境下就不會有鋼筋腐蝕問題。","假設鋼線直徑 7 mm、抗拉強度 1,770 MPa：499 根 A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm²，破斷力約 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN，0.45 倍約 15,300 kN。"],"optionsEn":["If a wind-tunnel model is geometrically correct, its results scale directly to the full bridge.","High-strength concrete alone prevents reinforcement corrosion in seawater.","Assuming 7 mm wires of 1,770 MPa: 499 wires give A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm² and a breaking force of about 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN, with 0.45 of that about 15,300 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設鋼線直徑 7 mm、抗拉強度 1,770 MPa：499 根 A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm²，破斷力約 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN，0.45 倍約 15,300 kN；163 根 A ≈ 6,270 mm²，破斷力約 11,100 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assuming 7 mm wires of 1,770 MPa: 499 wires give A = 499×38.48 ≈ 19,200 mm² and a breaking force of about 19,200×1,770 ≈ 34,000 kN, with 0.45 of that about 15,300 kN; 163 wires give A ≈ 6,270 mm² and about 11,100 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b009-v13-15","title":"224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塔內錨箱」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tower anchor boxes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"斜索與錨具依斜索規範做組裝體疲勞、破斷與防水試驗，並在 1:1 索段做風雨振試驗；錨箱焊道以超音波檢測，安裝後量測每根索的最終力與錨頭位置，與設計表逐一比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test stay and anchorage assemblies for fatigue, ultimate strength and watertightness under stay-cable recommendations, and test full-scale cable sections for wind and rain vibration; inspect anchor-box welds ultrasonically and after installation compare each stay’s final force and anchor-head position with the design table. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時要留下每根索的編號、鋼線數、外徑、設計與實測索力、錨具型號及出廠試驗報告；錨箱內要設照明、通風與檢查通道，確保日後能接近錨頭。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover keep each stay’s number, wire count, diameter, design and measured force, anchorage type and test reports; anchor boxes need lighting, ventilation and access so anchor heads can be reached later.","failure":"注意干擾：錨箱焊道或承壓板細節不當時，反覆的索力變化會在焊趾處產生疲勞裂縫；錨頭防水失效則讓水進入索內，鋼線在錨口附近腐蝕，這個位置正是目視最難檢查的地方。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Poor anchor-box welds or bearing-plate details let repeated force changes start fatigue cracks at weld toes; failed anchor-head sealing lets water into the cable and corrodes wires near the socket, exactly where visual inspection is hardest. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"斜索與錨具依斜索規範做組裝體疲勞、破斷與防水試驗，並在 1:1 索段做風雨振試驗；錨箱焊道以超音波檢測，安裝後量測每根索的最終力與錨頭位置，與設計表逐一比對。","textEn":"Test stay and anchorage assemblies for fatigue, ultimate strength and watertightness under stay-cable recommendations, and test full-scale cable sections for wind and rain vibration; inspect anchor-box welds ultrasonically and after installation compare each stay’s final force and anchor-head position with the design table.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時要留下每根索的編號、鋼線數、外徑、設計與實測索力、錨具型號及出廠試驗報告；錨箱內要設照明、通風與檢查通道，確保日後能接近錨頭。","textEn":"At handover keep each stay’s number, wire count, diameter, design and measured force, anchorage type and test reports; anchor boxes need lighting, ventilation and access so anchor heads can be reached later.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes\"?","options":["斜索與錨具依斜索規範做組裝體疲勞、破斷與防水試驗，並在 1:1 索段做風雨振試驗；錨箱焊道以超音波檢測，安裝後量測每根索的最終力與錨頭位置，與設計表逐一比對。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","橋面越寬越重，風就越吹不動，所以千米跨只要加重即可抗颱風。"],"optionsEn":["Test stay and anchorage assemblies for fatigue, ultimate strength and watertightness under stay-cable recommendations, and test full-scale cable sections for wind and rain vibration.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A wider, heavier deck is always harder for wind to move, so a 1 km span only needs more weight to resist typhoons."],"answer":0,"explanation":"斜索與錨具依斜索規範做組裝體疲勞、破斷與防水試驗，並在 1:1 索段做風雨振試驗；錨箱焊道以超音波檢測，安裝後量測每根索的最終力與錨頭位置，與設計表逐一比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test stay and anchorage assemblies for fatigue, ultimate strength and watertightness under stay-cable recommendations, and test full-scale cable sections for wind and rain vibration; inspect anchor-box welds ultrasonically and after installation compare each stay’s final force and anchor-head position with the design table. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b009-v13-16","title":"224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置：失效診斷","titleEn":"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塔內錨箱」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tower anchor boxes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錨箱焊道或承壓板細節不當時，反覆的索力變化會在焊趾處產生疲勞裂縫；錨頭防水失效則讓水進入索內，鋼線在錨口附近腐蝕，這個位置正是目視最難檢查的地方。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Poor anchor-box welds or bearing-plate details let repeated force changes start fatigue cracks at weld toes; failed anchor-head sealing lets water into the cable and corrodes wires near the socket, exactly where visual inspection is hardest. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：索徑與鋼線數的變化正好反映了扇形配置下索力的分布。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The change of diameter and wire count mirrors the force distribution in a fan arrangement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一座橋的斜拉索應該都一樣粗，才方便施工和維護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All stays on one bridge should have the same size for easier construction and maintenance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錨箱焊道或承壓板細節不當時，反覆的索力變化會在焊趾處產生疲勞裂縫；錨頭防水失效則讓水進入索內，鋼線在錨口附近腐蝕，這個位置正是目視最難檢查的地方。","textEn":"Poor anchor-box welds or bearing-plate details let repeated force changes start fatigue cracks at weld toes; failed anchor-head sealing lets water into the cable and corrodes wires near the socket, exactly where visual inspection is hardest.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「224 根斜拉索、錨箱與索徑配置」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The 224 stays, anchor boxes and cable sizes\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","錨箱焊道或承壓板細節不當時，反覆的索力變化會在焊趾處產生疲勞裂縫；錨頭防水失效則讓水進入索內，鋼線在錨口附近腐蝕，這個位置正是目視最難檢查的地方。","成橋狀態能抗颱風，施工中的懸臂狀態自然也能。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Poor anchor-box welds or bearing-plate details let repeated force changes start fatigue cracks at weld toes.","If the completed bridge resists typhoons, the cantilever stage naturally does too."],"answer":1,"explanation":"錨箱焊道或承壓板細節不當時，反覆的索力變化會在焊趾處產生疲勞裂縫；錨頭防水失效則讓水進入索內，鋼線在錨口附近腐蝕，這個位置正是目視最難檢查的地方。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Poor anchor-box welds or bearing-plate details let repeated force changes start fatigue cracks at weld toes; failed anchor-head sealing lets water into the cable and corrodes wires near the socket, exactly where visual inspection is hardest. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b009-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定」與「鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability\" and \"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b009-v13-17","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「起重門架與最大懸臂」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lifting gantries and maximum cantilever” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"昂船洲大橋主跨鋼梁在工廠分片製造、再組成節段，以駁船運到橋下，由懸臂端的起重門架垂直吊升，逐段焊接並安裝對應的斜索；靠近塔的一小段鋼梁則在臨時支架上架設。懸臂越伸越長時，結構是兩支各約 500 m 的懸臂，橫向只有塔與斜索支撐，對颱風最為脆弱；吊裝作業又受海峽航運與潮流限制。施工團隊必須規劃颱風來臨前的停工、門架固定與臨時抗風措施，並預估懸臂端在風中的位移與塔底的附加彎矩。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「起重門架與最大懸臂」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The main-span steel was fabricated as panels, assembled into segments, barged under the bridge and lifted vertically by gantries at the cantilever tips, each segment welded in and its stays installed; the short section next to each tower was erected on temporary falsework. As the cantilevers grow, the structure becomes two cantilevers of roughly 500 m supported laterally only by the tower and stays, its most typhoon-vulnerable state, while lifts are also constrained by channel shipping and currents. The team must plan stoppages, gantry tie-downs and temporary wind measures before a typhoon and predict cantilever-tip displacement and the added moment at the tower base. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Lifting gantries and maximum cantilever” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：懸臂受均布側風 w 時，塔處側向彎矩 M = w·L²/2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a cantilever under uniform side wind w, the lateral moment at the tower is M = w·L²/2.","failure":"常見誤解：「成橋狀態能抗颱風，施工中的懸臂狀態自然也能。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the completed bridge resists typhoons, the cantilever stage naturally does too.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「起重門架與最大懸臂」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Lifting gantries and maximum cantilever”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-17-k1","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定","titleEn":"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability","text":"昂船洲大橋主跨鋼梁在工廠分片製造、再組成節段，以駁船運到橋下，由懸臂端的起重門架垂直吊升，逐段焊接並安裝對應的斜索；靠近塔的一小段鋼梁則在臨時支架上架設。懸臂越伸越長時，結構是兩支各約 500 m 的懸臂，橫向只有塔與斜索支撐，對颱風最為脆弱；吊裝作業又受海峽航運與潮流限制。","textEn":"The main-span steel was fabricated as panels, assembled into segments, barged under the bridge and lifted vertically by gantries at the cantilever tips, each segment welded in and its stays installed; the short section next to each tower was erected on temporary falsework. As the cantilevers grow, the structure becomes two cantilevers of roughly 500 m supported laterally only by the tower and stays, its most typhoon-vulnerable state, while lifts are also constrained by channel shipping and currents.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：成橋狀態能抗颱風，施工中的懸臂狀態自然也能。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the completed bridge resists typhoons, the cantilever stage naturally does too. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability\" is correct?","options":["成橋狀態能抗颱風，施工中的懸臂狀態自然也能。","鋼梁與混凝土梁只要用螺栓頭對頭接上，力量就會平均傳遞。","昂船洲大橋主跨鋼梁在工廠分片製造、再組成節段，以駁船運到橋下，由懸臂端的起重門架垂直吊升，逐段焊接並安裝對應的斜索；靠近塔的一小段鋼梁則在臨時支架上架設。"],"optionsEn":["If the completed bridge resists typhoons, the cantilever stage naturally does too.","Bolting the steel girder end to the concrete girder end transfers force evenly.","The main-span steel was fabricated as panels, assembled into segments, barged under the bridge and lifted vertically by gantries at the cantilever tips, each segment welded in and its stays installed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"昂船洲大橋主跨鋼梁在工廠分片製造、再組成節段，以駁船運到橋下，由懸臂端的起重門架垂直吊升，逐段焊接並安裝對應的斜索；靠近塔的一小段鋼梁則在臨時支架上架設。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The main-span steel was fabricated as panels, assembled into segments, barged under the bridge and lifted vertically by gantries at the cantilever tips, each segment welded in and its stays installed; the short section next to each tower was erected on temporary falsework. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b009-v13-18","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定：定量估算","titleEn":"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「起重門架與最大懸臂」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lifting gantries and maximum cantilever” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：懸臂受均布側風 w 時，塔處側向彎矩 M = w·L²/2。取 w = 4.9 kN/m、L = 500 m：M = 4.9×500²/2 ≈ 612,500 kN·m；若施工期設計風速使 w 降為 3.9 kN/m，M ≈ 490,000 kN·m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a cantilever under uniform side wind w, the lateral moment at the tower is M = w·L²/2. With w = 4.9 kN/m and L = 500 m, M = 4.9×500²/2 ≈ 612,500 kN·m; if the construction-stage design wind reduces w to 3.9 kN/m, M ≈ 490,000 kN·m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：施工階段分析逐一檢查每個懸臂長度下的抗風安全與顫振臨界風速，並在現場設風速計與懸臂端 GNSS；每次吊裝前確認風速、潮流與航道封閉，門架與吊具由第三方檢驗，吊裝後量測節段高程與斜索力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The staged analysis checks wind safety and flutter speed at each cantilever length, with anemometers and GNSS at the tip on site; before each lift confirm wind, current and channel closure, have gantries and rigging third-party inspected, and after the lift measure segment levels and stay forces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"懸臂受均布側風 w 時，塔處側向彎矩 M = w·L²/2。取 w = 4.9 kN/m、L = 500 m：M = 4.9×500²/2 ≈ 612,500 kN·m；若施工期設計風速使 w 降為 3.9 kN/m，M ≈ 490,000 kN·m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a cantilever under uniform side wind w, the lateral moment at the tower is M = w·L²/2. With w = 4.9 kN/m and L = 500 m, M = 4.9×500²/2 ≈ 612,500 kN·m; if the construction-stage design wind reduces w to 3.9 kN/m, M ≈ 490,000 kN·m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability\", which statement holds?","options":["懸臂受均布側風 w 時，塔處側向彎矩 M = w·L²/2。","大橋跨中撓度達到一兩公尺，就表示結構不安全。","斜拉索索力一旦施工完成就不會再改變，不需要追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["For a cantilever under uniform side wind w, the lateral moment at the tower is M = w·L²/2.","A mid-span deflection of one or two metres means the bridge is unsafe.","Stay forces never change after construction, so they need no tracking."],"answer":0,"explanation":"懸臂受均布側風 w 時，塔處側向彎矩 M = w·L²/2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a cantilever under uniform side wind w, the lateral moment at the tower is M = w·L²/2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b009-v13-19","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「起重門架與最大懸臂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lifting gantries and maximum cantilever” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"施工階段分析逐一檢查每個懸臂長度下的抗風安全與顫振臨界風速，並在現場設風速計與懸臂端 GNSS；每次吊裝前確認風速、潮流與航道封閉，門架與吊具由第三方檢驗，吊裝後量測節段高程與斜索力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The staged analysis checks wind safety and flutter speed at each cantilever length, with anemometers and GNSS at the tip on site; before each lift confirm wind, current and channel closure, have gantries and rigging third-party inspected, and after the lift measure segment levels and stay forces. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工計畫要訂出各懸臂長度的作業風速上限、颱風警報分級對應的固定程序與人員撤離時點，並把最大懸臂的抗風措施列為停留檢查點，由設計與施工工程師共同確認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The method statement should set working wind limits for each cantilever length, securing procedures and evacuation times for each typhoon-signal level, with the maximum-cantilever wind measures a hold point confirmed jointly by the design and construction engineers.","failure":"注意干擾：颱風預警時若懸臂端門架或未焊完的節段沒有可靠固定，強風可能使吊具擺動撞擊結構；最大懸臂狀態下若臨時抗風措施不足，側向位移與塔底彎矩可能超出設計，甚至出現施工期的氣彈振動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If gantries or partly welded segments at the tip are not secured when a typhoon warning is issued, rigging can swing into the structure; at the maximum cantilever, inadequate temporary wind measures can push lateral displacement and tower-base moment beyond design or even trigger construction-stage aeroelastic motion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"施工階段分析逐一檢查每個懸臂長度下的抗風安全與顫振臨界風速，並在現場設風速計與懸臂端 GNSS；每次吊裝前確認風速、潮流與航道封閉，門架與吊具由第三方檢驗，吊裝後量測節段高程與斜索力。","textEn":"The staged analysis checks wind safety and flutter speed at each cantilever length, with anemometers and GNSS at the tip on site; before each lift confirm wind, current and channel closure, have gantries and rigging third-party inspected, and after the lift measure segment levels and stay forces.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工計畫要訂出各懸臂長度的作業風速上限、颱風警報分級對應的固定程序與人員撤離時點，並把最大懸臂的抗風措施列為停留檢查點，由設計與施工工程師共同確認。","textEn":"The method statement should set working wind limits for each cantilever length, securing procedures and evacuation times for each typhoon-signal level, with the maximum-cantilever wind measures a hold point confirmed jointly by the design and construction engineers.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","施工階段分析逐一檢查每個懸臂長度下的抗風安全與顫振臨界風速，並在現場設風速計與懸臂端 GNSS。","塔梁之間只要用固定支承鎖死，橋就最穩。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","The staged analysis checks wind safety and flutter speed at each cantilever length, with anemometers and GNSS at the tip on site.","Fixing the deck rigidly to the tower always makes the bridge most stable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"施工階段分析逐一檢查每個懸臂長度下的抗風安全與顫振臨界風速，並在現場設風速計與懸臂端 GNSS；每次吊裝前確認風速、潮流與航道封閉，門架與吊具由第三方檢驗，吊裝後量測節段高程與斜索力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The staged analysis checks wind safety and flutter speed at each cantilever length, with anemometers and GNSS at the tip on site; before each lift confirm wind, current and channel closure, have gantries and rigging third-party inspected, and after the lift measure segment levels and stay forces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b009-v13-20","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「起重門架與最大懸臂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lifting gantries and maximum cantilever” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"颱風預警時若懸臂端門架或未焊完的節段沒有可靠固定，強風可能使吊具擺動撞擊結構；最大懸臂狀態下若臨時抗風措施不足，側向位移與塔底彎矩可能超出設計，甚至出現施工期的氣彈振動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If gantries or partly welded segments at the tip are not secured when a typhoon warning is issued, rigging can swing into the structure; at the maximum cantilever, inadequate temporary wind measures can push lateral displacement and tower-base moment beyond design or even trigger construction-stage aeroelastic motion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：施工團隊必須規劃颱風來臨前的停工、門架固定與臨時抗風措施，並預估懸臂端在風中的位移與塔底的附加彎矩。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The team must plan stoppages, gantry tie-downs and temporary wind measures before a typhoon and predict cantilever-tip displacement and the added moment at the tower base.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「成橋狀態能抗颱風，施工中的懸臂狀態自然也能。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the completed bridge resists typhoons, the cantilever stage naturally does too.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"颱風預警時若懸臂端門架或未焊完的節段沒有可靠固定，強風可能使吊具擺動撞擊結構；最大懸臂狀態下若臨時抗風措施不足，側向位移與塔底彎矩可能超出設計，甚至出現施工期的氣彈振動。","textEn":"If gantries or partly welded segments at the tip are not secured when a typhoon warning is issued, rigging can swing into the structure; at the maximum cantilever, inadequate temporary wind measures can push lateral displacement and tower-base moment beyond design or even trigger construction-stage aeroelastic motion.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與颱風季臨時穩定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cantilever lifting of steel boxes and typhoon-season stability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","鋼梁與混凝土梁只要用螺栓頭對頭接上，力量就會平均傳遞。","颱風預警時若懸臂端門架或未焊完的節段沒有可靠固定，強風可能使吊具擺動撞擊結構。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Bolting the steel girder end to the concrete girder end transfers force evenly.","If gantries or partly welded segments at the tip are not secured when a typhoon warning is issued, rigging can swing into the structure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"颱風預警時若懸臂端門架或未焊完的節段沒有可靠固定，強風可能使吊具擺動撞擊結構；最大懸臂狀態下若臨時抗風措施不足，側向位移與塔底彎矩可能超出設計，甚至出現施工期的氣彈振動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If gantries or partly welded segments at the tip are not secured when a typhoon warning is issued, rigging can swing into the structure; at the maximum cantilever, inadequate temporary wind measures can push lateral displacement and tower-base moment beyond design or even trigger construction-stage aeroelastic motion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b009-v13-21","title":"鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「背跨鋼混接頭」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Back-span steel–concrete junction” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"昂船洲大橋的鋼主梁並不在塔處結束，而是伸入背跨約 49.75 m 後才與混凝土雙箱梁接合。接頭位置選在彎矩與剪力相對溫和處，但仍要傳遞斜索在橋面累積的巨大水平壓力、彎矩與剪力。常見做法是在鋼梁端部設承壓板與格室，內部填混凝土，以剪力釘、開孔鋼板連接件與預力鋼腱把鋼與混凝土綁成一體。接頭兩側勁度差異很大，溫度、乾縮與徐變都會在界面集中應力，因此是全橋細部最複雜的區域之一。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「背跨鋼混接頭」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Stonecutters steel girder does not stop at the towers; it extends about 49.75 m into each back span before joining the concrete twin boxes. The junction is placed where moment and shear are relatively moderate but must still transfer the large horizontal compression accumulated from the stays, plus moment and shear. A common solution uses end bearing plates and cells filled with concrete, with shear studs, perforated-plate connectors and prestressing tendons binding steel and concrete together. Stiffness changes sharply across the junction, and temperature, shrinkage and creep concentrate stress at the interface, making it one of the most complex details of the bridge. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Back-span steel–concrete junction” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若接頭需傳遞 100 MN 的水平壓力，其中由剪力釘承擔的部分以每支 150 kN 的設計強度計，需約 100,000/150 ≈ 667 支；若改由承壓板直接承擔一半，剪力釘只需約 334 支。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If the junction must transfer 100 MN of horizontal compression and studs carry it at 150 kN design resistance each, about 100,000/150 ≈ 667 studs are needed; if bearing plates take half directly, only about 334 studs are needed.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼梁與混凝土梁只要用螺栓頭對頭接上，力量就會平均傳遞。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Bolting the steel girder end to the concrete girder end transfers force evenly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「背跨鋼混接頭」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Back-span steel–concrete junction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-21-k1","title":"鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞","titleEn":"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction","text":"昂船洲大橋的鋼主梁並不在塔處結束，而是伸入背跨約 49.75 m 後才與混凝土雙箱梁接合。接頭位置選在彎矩與剪力相對溫和處，但仍要傳遞斜索在橋面累積的巨大水平壓力、彎矩與剪力。","textEn":"The Stonecutters steel girder does not stop at the towers; it extends about 49.75 m into each back span before joining the concrete twin boxes. The junction is placed where moment and shear are relatively moderate but must still transfer the large horizontal compression accumulated from the stays, plus moment and shear.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼梁與混凝土梁只要用螺栓頭對頭接上，力量就會平均傳遞。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Bolting the steel girder end to the concrete girder end transfers force evenly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction\" is correct?","options":["昂船洲大橋的鋼主梁並不在塔處結束，而是伸入背跨約 49.75 m 後才與混凝土雙箱梁接合。","鋼梁與混凝土梁只要用螺栓頭對頭接上，力量就會平均傳遞。","風洞模型只要幾何縮尺正確，試驗結果就能直接放大套用到實橋。"],"optionsEn":["The Stonecutters steel girder does not stop at the towers; it extends about 49.75 m into each back span before joining the concrete twin boxes.","Bolting the steel girder end to the concrete girder end transfers force evenly.","If a wind-tunnel model is geometrically correct, its results scale directly to the full bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"昂船洲大橋的鋼主梁並不在塔處結束，而是伸入背跨約 49.75 m 後才與混凝土雙箱梁接合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Stonecutters steel girder does not stop at the towers; it extends about 49.75 m into each back span before joining the concrete twin boxes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b009-v13-22","title":"鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞：定量估算","titleEn":"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「背跨鋼混接頭」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Back-span steel–concrete junction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若接頭需傳遞 100 MN 的水平壓力，其中由剪力釘承擔的部分以每支 150 kN 的設計強度計，需約 100,000/150 ≈ 667 支；若改由承壓板直接承擔一半，剪力釘只需約 334 支。力量與釘強度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If the junction must transfer 100 MN of horizontal compression and studs carry it at 150 kN design resistance each, about 100,000/150 ≈ 667 studs are needed; if bearing plates take half directly, only about 334 studs are needed. Force and stud resistance are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以局部有限元素模型分析承壓板、格室與連接件的應力分布，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證荷重—滑移行為；現場檢查剪力釘焊接（彎曲試驗）、格室混凝土密實度與預力鋼腱的伸長量紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Analyse bearing plates, cells and connectors with a local finite-element model and verify load–slip behaviour on scaled or full-size specimens; on site check stud welds by bend testing, concrete compaction in the cells and elongation records of the tendons.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若接頭需傳遞 100 MN 的水平壓力，其中由剪力釘承擔的部分以每支 150 kN 的設計強度計，需約 100,000/150 ≈ 667 支；若改由承壓板直接承擔一半，剪力釘只需約 334 支。力量與釘強度為教學假設。","textEn":"If the junction must transfer 100 MN of horizontal compression and studs carry it at 150 kN design resistance each, about 100,000/150 ≈ 667 studs are needed; if bearing plates take half directly, only about 334 studs are needed. Force and stud resistance are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction\", which statement holds?","options":["只要混凝土強度高，海水環境下就不會有鋼筋腐蝕問題。","若接頭需傳遞 100 MN 的水平壓力，其中由剪力釘承擔的部分以每支 150 kN 的設計強度計，需約 100,000/150 ≈ 667 支。","橋面越寬越重，風就越吹不動，所以千米跨只要加重即可抗颱風。"],"optionsEn":["High-strength concrete alone prevents reinforcement corrosion in seawater.","If the junction must transfer 100 MN of horizontal compression and studs carry it at 150 kN design resistance each, about 100,000/150 ≈ 667 studs are needed.","A wider, heavier deck is always harder for wind to move, so a 1 km span only needs more weight to resist typhoons."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若接頭需傳遞 100 MN 的水平壓力，其中由剪力釘承擔的部分以每支 150 kN 的設計強度計，需約 100,000/150 ≈ 667 支；若改由承壓板直接承擔一半，剪力釘只需約 334 支。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If the junction must transfer 100 MN of horizontal compression and studs carry it at 150 kN design resistance each, about 100,000/150 ≈ 667 studs are needed; if bearing plates take half directly, only about 334 studs are needed. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b009-v13-23","title":"鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「背跨鋼混接頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Back-span steel–concrete junction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以局部有限元素模型分析承壓板、格室與連接件的應力分布，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證荷重—滑移行為；現場檢查剪力釘焊接（彎曲試驗）、格室混凝土密實度與預力鋼腱的伸長量紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Analyse bearing plates, cells and connectors with a local finite-element model and verify load–slip behaviour on scaled or full-size specimens; on site check stud welds by bend testing, concrete compaction in the cells and elongation records of the tendons. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：接頭格室的混凝土澆置要有排氣孔與觀察孔，並以試拌與模擬澆置確認流動性；施工紀錄要保存剪力釘檢測與預力張拉資料，作為日後評估接頭狀態的依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Cells at the junction need vent and inspection holes, with flowability proven by trial mixes and mock-up pours; keep stud-test and tendon-stressing records as the basis for later condition assessment of the junction.","failure":"注意干擾：格室混凝土不密實或剪力釘焊接不良，會讓接頭出現界面滑移與裂縫，水分沿界面滲入造成鋼材與鋼筋腐蝕；長期徐變重分配若未納入設計，接頭附近的混凝土可能開裂，鋼梁端部出現疲勞熱點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Poorly compacted cell concrete or bad stud welds let the interface slip and crack, admitting water that corrodes steel and reinforcement; if long-term creep redistribution is not designed for, concrete near the junction can crack and fatigue hot spots appear at the steel ends. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以局部有限元素模型分析承壓板、格室與連接件的應力分布，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證荷重—滑移行為；現場檢查剪力釘焊接（彎曲試驗）、格室混凝土密實度與預力鋼腱的伸長量紀錄。","textEn":"Analyse bearing plates, cells and connectors with a local finite-element model and verify load–slip behaviour on scaled or full-size specimens; on site check stud welds by bend testing, concrete compaction in the cells and elongation records of the tendons.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"接頭格室的混凝土澆置要有排氣孔與觀察孔，並以試拌與模擬澆置確認流動性；施工紀錄要保存剪力釘檢測與預力張拉資料，作為日後評估接頭狀態的依據。","textEn":"Cells at the junction need vent and inspection holes, with flowability proven by trial mixes and mock-up pours; keep stud-test and tendon-stressing records as the basis for later condition assessment of the junction.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","不鏽鋼外皮只是為了外觀好看，不參與結構受力。","以局部有限元素模型分析承壓板、格室與連接件的應力分布，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證荷重—滑移行為。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The stainless skin is only for appearance and carries no structural load.","Analyse bearing plates, cells and connectors with a local finite-element model and verify load–slip behaviour on scaled or full-size specimens."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以局部有限元素模型分析承壓板、格室與連接件的應力分布，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證荷重—滑移行為；現場檢查剪力釘焊接（彎曲試驗）、格室混凝土密實度與預力鋼腱的伸長量紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Analyse bearing plates, cells and connectors with a local finite-element model and verify load–slip behaviour on scaled or full-size specimens; on site check stud welds by bend testing, concrete compaction in the cells and elongation records of the tendons. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b009-v13-24","title":"鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「背跨鋼混接頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Back-span steel–concrete junction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"格室混凝土不密實或剪力釘焊接不良，會讓接頭出現界面滑移與裂縫，水分沿界面滲入造成鋼材與鋼筋腐蝕；長期徐變重分配若未納入設計，接頭附近的混凝土可能開裂，鋼梁端部出現疲勞熱點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Poorly compacted cell concrete or bad stud welds let the interface slip and crack, admitting water that corrodes steel and reinforcement; if long-term creep redistribution is not designed for, concrete near the junction can crack and fatigue hot spots appear at the steel ends. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：接頭兩側勁度差異很大，溫度、乾縮與徐變都會在界面集中應力，因此是全橋細部最複雜的區域之一。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Stiffness changes sharply across the junction, and temperature, shrinkage and creep concentrate stress at the interface, making it one of the most complex details of the bridge.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼梁與混凝土梁只要用螺栓頭對頭接上，力量就會平均傳遞。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Bolting the steel girder end to the concrete girder end transfers force evenly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"格室混凝土不密實或剪力釘焊接不良，會讓接頭出現界面滑移與裂縫，水分沿界面滲入造成鋼材與鋼筋腐蝕；長期徐變重分配若未納入設計，接頭附近的混凝土可能開裂，鋼梁端部出現疲勞熱點。","textEn":"Poorly compacted cell concrete or bad stud welds let the interface slip and crack, admitting water that corrodes steel and reinforcement; if long-term creep redistribution is not designed for, concrete near the junction can crack and fatigue hot spots appear at the steel ends.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼—混凝土接合段的力量傳遞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Force transfer at the steel–concrete junction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["格室混凝土不密實或剪力釘焊接不良，會讓接頭出現界面滑移與裂縫，水分沿界面滲入造成鋼材與鋼筋腐蝕。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","風洞模型只要幾何縮尺正確，試驗結果就能直接放大套用到實橋。"],"optionsEn":["Poorly compacted cell concrete or bad stud welds let the interface slip and crack, admitting water that corrodes steel and reinforcement.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If a wind-tunnel model is geometrically correct, its results scale directly to the full bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"格室混凝土不密實或剪力釘焊接不良，會讓接頭出現界面滑移與裂縫，水分沿界面滲入造成鋼材與鋼筋腐蝕；長期徐變重分配若未納入設計，接頭附近的混凝土可能開裂，鋼梁端部出現疲勞熱點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Poorly compacted cell concrete or bad stud welds let the interface slip and crack, admitting water that corrodes steel and reinforcement; if long-term creep redistribution is not designed for, concrete near the junction can crack and fatigue hot spots appear at the steel ends. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b009-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形」與「跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain\" and \"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b009-v13-25","title":"多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「雷諾數效應」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reynolds-number effects” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"公開設計資料指出，昂船洲大橋做了 1:80 與 1:20 兩種比例的橋面斷面風洞試驗、1:1 的斜索試驗以及 1:1,500 的地形模型試驗。原因在於風洞模型無法同時滿足所有相似律：小比例模型的雷諾數比實橋小數百倍，流線形箱梁圓角處的分離點可能與實橋不同，使渦振與氣動係數失真；較大的 1:20 模型提高雷諾數以檢核這種敏感性。地形模型則用來取得周邊山體與城市對來風的紊流與風速剖面，作為斷面試驗的輸入。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「雷諾數效應」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Published design data state that Stonecutters Bridge was tested with deck section models at 1:80 and 1:20, full-scale 1:1 stay tests and a 1:1,500 terrain model. No wind-tunnel model can satisfy every similarity law: a small model’s Reynolds number is hundreds of times below full scale, so flow separation at the rounded corners of a streamlined box may differ from reality and distort vortex response and aerodynamic coefficients; the larger 1:20 model raises the Reynolds number to check this sensitivity. The terrain model provides turbulence and wind profiles from the surrounding hills and city as input to the section tests. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Reynolds-number effects” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：雷諾數 Re = U·D/ν，ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Reynolds number Re = U·D/ν with ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「風洞模型只要幾何縮尺正確，試驗結果就能直接放大套用到實橋。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If a wind-tunnel model is geometrically correct, its results scale directly to the full bridge.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「雷諾數效應」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Reynolds-number effects”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-25-k1","title":"多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形","titleEn":"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain","text":"公開設計資料指出，昂船洲大橋做了 1:80 與 1:20 兩種比例的橋面斷面風洞試驗、1:1 的斜索試驗以及 1:1,500 的地形模型試驗。原因在於風洞模型無法同時滿足所有相似律：小比例模型的雷諾數比實橋小數百倍，流線形箱梁圓角處的分離點可能與實橋不同，使渦振與氣動係數失真；較大的 1:20 模型提高雷諾數以檢核這種敏感性。","textEn":"Published design data state that Stonecutters Bridge was tested with deck section models at 1:80 and 1:20, full-scale 1:1 stay tests and a 1:1,500 terrain model. No wind-tunnel model can satisfy every similarity law: a small model’s Reynolds number is hundreds of times below full scale, so flow separation at the rounded corners of a streamlined box may differ from reality and distort vortex response and aerodynamic coefficients; the larger 1:20 model raises the Reynolds number to check this sensitivity.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風洞模型只要幾何縮尺正確，試驗結果就能直接放大套用到實橋。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If a wind-tunnel model is geometrically correct, its results scale directly to the full bridge. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain\" is correct?","options":["風洞模型只要幾何縮尺正確，試驗結果就能直接放大套用到實橋。","公開設計資料指出，昂船洲大橋做了 1:80 與 1:20 兩種比例的橋面斷面風洞試驗、1:1 的斜索試驗以及 1:1,500 的地形模型試驗。","大橋跨中撓度達到一兩公尺，就表示結構不安全。"],"optionsEn":["If a wind-tunnel model is geometrically correct, its results scale directly to the full bridge.","Published design data state that Stonecutters Bridge was tested with deck section models at 1:80 and 1:20, full-scale 1:1 stay tests and a 1:1,500 terrain model.","A mid-span deflection of one or two metres means the bridge is unsafe."],"answer":1,"explanation":"公開設計資料指出，昂船洲大橋做了 1:80 與 1:20 兩種比例的橋面斷面風洞試驗、1:1 的斜索試驗以及 1:1,500 的地形模型試驗。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Published design data state that Stonecutters Bridge was tested with deck section models at 1:80 and 1:20, full-scale 1:1 stay tests and a 1:1,500 terrain model. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b009-v13-26","title":"多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形：定量估算","titleEn":"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雷諾數效應」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reynolds-number effects” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：雷諾數 Re = U·D/ν，ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s。1:80 模型 D = 0.05 m、U = 10 m/s：Re ≈ 3.3×10⁴；實橋 D = 4 m、U = 50 m/s：Re ≈ 1.3×10⁷，相差約 400 倍；1:20 模型 D = 0.2 m、U = 10 m/s 時 Re ≈ 1.3×10⁵，差距縮小到約 100 倍。尺寸與風速為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Reynolds number Re = U·D/ν with ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s. A 1:80 model with D = 0.05 m at 10 m/s gives Re ≈ 3.3×10⁴; the bridge with D = 4 m at 50 m/s gives Re ≈ 1.3×10⁷, about 400 times higher; a 1:20 model with D = 0.2 m at 10 m/s gives Re ≈ 1.3×10⁵, narrowing the gap to about 100 times. Dimensions and speeds are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較兩種比例模型在相同折算風速下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，若差異顯著，以較大比例或表面粗糙化處理推估實橋行為；地形模型量測的紊流強度與積分尺度要與現場風速計長期資料互相校核。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes of the two model scales at the same reduced velocity; where they differ significantly, infer full-scale behaviour from the larger scale or with surface roughening; cross-check turbulence intensity and integral scales from the terrain model against long-term site anemometer data.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"雷諾數 Re = U·D/ν，ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s。1:80 模型 D = 0.05 m、U = 10 m/s：Re ≈ 3.3×10⁴；實橋 D = 4 m、U = 50 m/s：Re ≈ 1.3×10⁷，相差約 400 倍；1:20 模型 D = 0.2 m、U = 10 m/s 時 Re ≈ 1.3×10⁵，差距縮小到約 100 倍。尺寸與風速為教學假設。","textEn":"Reynolds number Re = U·D/ν with ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s. A 1:80 model with D = 0.05 m at 10 m/s gives Re ≈ 3.3×10⁴; the bridge with D = 4 m at 50 m/s gives Re ≈ 1.3×10⁷, about 400 times higher; a 1:20 model with D = 0.2 m at 10 m/s gives Re ≈ 1.3×10⁵, narrowing the gap to about 100 times. Dimensions and speeds are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain\", which statement holds?","options":["斜拉索索力一旦施工完成就不會再改變，不需要追蹤。","塔梁之間只要用固定支承鎖死，橋就最穩。","雷諾數 Re = U·D/ν，ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s。"],"optionsEn":["Stay forces never change after construction, so they need no tracking.","Fixing the deck rigidly to the tower always makes the bridge most stable.","Reynolds number Re = U·D/ν with ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雷諾數 Re = U·D/ν，ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Reynolds number Re = U·D/ν with ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b009-v13-27","title":"多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雷諾數效應」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reynolds-number effects” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較兩種比例模型在相同折算風速下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，若差異顯著，以較大比例或表面粗糙化處理推估實橋行為；地形模型量測的紊流強度與積分尺度要與現場風速計長期資料互相校核。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes of the two model scales at the same reduced velocity; where they differ significantly, infer full-scale behaviour from the larger scale or with surface roughening; cross-check turbulence intensity and integral scales from the terrain model against long-term site anemometer data. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：風洞試驗規範應寫明模型比例、相似律取捨、雷諾數敏感性檢核與附屬物細節；通車後安排實橋風速與加速度監測，回饋驗證試驗推估。","observationEn":"Site practice: The wind-testing specification should state model scales, which similarity laws are relaxed, Reynolds-sensitivity checks and attachment details; after opening, arrange full-scale wind and acceleration monitoring to validate the test predictions.","failure":"注意干擾：若只依小比例模型認定沒有渦振，實橋在較高雷諾數下的分離行為改變，可能出現模型未預測的振動；反之也可能因模型過度保守而增加不必要的導流板或阻尼裝置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Relying on a small model alone to rule out vortex vibration can miss oscillation that appears at full-scale Reynolds numbers where separation changes; the opposite error adds unnecessary fairings or dampers because the model was over-conservative. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較兩種比例模型在相同折算風速下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，若差異顯著，以較大比例或表面粗糙化處理推估實橋行為；地形模型量測的紊流強度與積分尺度要與現場風速計長期資料互相校核。","textEn":"Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes of the two model scales at the same reduced velocity; where they differ significantly, infer full-scale behaviour from the larger scale or with surface roughening; cross-check turbulence intensity and integral scales from the terrain model against long-term site anemometer data.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"風洞試驗規範應寫明模型比例、相似律取捨、雷諾數敏感性檢核與附屬物細節；通車後安排實橋風速與加速度監測，回饋驗證試驗推估。","textEn":"The wind-testing specification should state model scales, which similarity laws are relaxed, Reynolds-sensitivity checks and attachment details; after opening, arrange full-scale wind and acceleration monitoring to validate the test predictions.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain\"?","options":["比較兩種比例模型在相同折算風速下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，若差異顯著，以較大比例或表面粗糙化處理推估實橋行為。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","同一座橋的斜拉索應該都一樣粗，才方便施工和維護。"],"optionsEn":["Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes of the two model scales at the same reduced velocity.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","All stays on one bridge should have the same size for easier construction and maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較兩種比例模型在相同折算風速下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，若差異顯著，以較大比例或表面粗糙化處理推估實橋行為；地形模型量測的紊流強度與積分尺度要與現場風速計長期資料互相校核。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes of the two model scales at the same reduced velocity; where they differ significantly, infer full-scale behaviour from the larger scale or with surface roughening; cross-check turbulence intensity and integral scales from the terrain model against long-term site anemometer data. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b009-v13-28","title":"多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形：失效診斷","titleEn":"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雷諾數效應」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reynolds-number effects” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只依小比例模型認定沒有渦振，實橋在較高雷諾數下的分離行為改變，可能出現模型未預測的振動；反之也可能因模型過度保守而增加不必要的導流板或阻尼裝置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Relying on a small model alone to rule out vortex vibration can miss oscillation that appears at full-scale Reynolds numbers where separation changes; the opposite error adds unnecessary fairings or dampers because the model was over-conservative. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地形模型則用來取得周邊山體與城市對來風的紊流與風速剖面，作為斷面試驗的輸入。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The terrain model provides turbulence and wind profiles from the surrounding hills and city as input to the section tests.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風洞模型只要幾何縮尺正確，試驗結果就能直接放大套用到實橋。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If a wind-tunnel model is geometrically correct, its results scale directly to the full bridge.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只依小比例模型認定沒有渦振，實橋在較高雷諾數下的分離行為改變，可能出現模型未預測的振動；反之也可能因模型過度保守而增加不必要的導流板或阻尼裝置。","textEn":"Relying on a small model alone to rule out vortex vibration can miss oscillation that appears at full-scale Reynolds numbers where separation changes; the opposite error adds unnecessary fairings or dampers because the model was over-conservative.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「多尺度風洞試驗：斷面、索與地形」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Multi-scale wind testing: section, cable and terrain\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只依小比例模型認定沒有渦振，實橋在較高雷諾數下的分離行為改變，可能出現模型未預測的振動；反之也可能因模型過度保守而增加不必要的導流板或阻尼裝置。","大橋跨中撓度達到一兩公尺，就表示結構不安全。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Relying on a small model alone to rule out vortex vibration can miss oscillation that appears at full-scale Reynolds numbers where separation changes.","A mid-span deflection of one or two metres means the bridge is unsafe."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只依小比例模型認定沒有渦振，實橋在較高雷諾數下的分離行為改變，可能出現模型未預測的振動；反之也可能因模型過度保守而增加不必要的導流板或阻尼裝置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Relying on a small model alone to rule out vortex vibration can miss oscillation that appears at full-scale Reynolds numbers where separation changes; the opposite error adds unnecessary fairings or dampers because the model was over-conservative. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b009-v13-29","title":"跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「跨中 GNSS 測點」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mid-span GNSS stations” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"香港路政署公開資料指出，昂船洲大橋跨中在交通荷載下撓度可達約 1.8 m，在風荷載下可達約 2.2 m。這樣大的位移是千米跨斜張橋的正常行為，而非缺陷，但也代表伸縮縫、支承、緩衝器與路面都必須容許相應的變形。監測系統以 GNSS、加速度計、應變計、溫度計與風速計記錄橋梁反應，工程師要把實測撓度依溫度、交通與風況分類，才能和設計預測公平比較，並從長期趨勢找出支承卡滯、索力變化或基礎沉陷的徵兆。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「跨中 GNSS 測點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hong Kong Highways Department data state that Stonecutters Bridge can deflect about 1.8 m at mid-span under traffic and about 2.2 m under wind. Such movements are normal for a 1 km cable-stayed span, not defects, but they require joints, bearings, buffers and surfacing to accommodate them. The monitoring system records response with GNSS, accelerometers, strain gauges, thermometers and anemometers, and engineers must sort measured deflections by temperature, traffic and wind before comparing them fairly with predictions, then look for signs of seized bearings, stay-force change or foundation settlement in long-term trends. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Mid-span GNSS stations” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：撓跨比：交通 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566，風 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Deflection-to-span ratios are 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566 for traffic and 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463 for wind.","failure":"常見誤解：「大橋跨中撓度達到一兩公尺，就表示結構不安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A mid-span deflection of one or two metres means the bridge is unsafe.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「跨中 GNSS 測點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Mid-span GNSS stations”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-29-k1","title":"跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀","titleEn":"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation","text":"香港路政署公開資料指出，昂船洲大橋跨中在交通荷載下撓度可達約 1.8 m，在風荷載下可達約 2.2 m。這樣大的位移是千米跨斜張橋的正常行為，而非缺陷，但也代表伸縮縫、支承、緩衝器與路面都必須容許相應的變形。","textEn":"Hong Kong Highways Department data state that Stonecutters Bridge can deflect about 1.8 m at mid-span under traffic and about 2.2 m under wind. Such movements are normal for a 1 km cable-stayed span, not defects, but they require joints, bearings, buffers and surfacing to accommodate them.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：大橋跨中撓度達到一兩公尺，就表示結構不安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A mid-span deflection of one or two metres means the bridge is unsafe. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation\" is correct?","options":["大橋跨中撓度達到一兩公尺，就表示結構不安全。","只要混凝土強度高，海水環境下就不會有鋼筋腐蝕問題。","香港路政署公開資料指出，昂船洲大橋跨中在交通荷載下撓度可達約 1.8 m，在風荷載下可達約 2.2 m。"],"optionsEn":["A mid-span deflection of one or two metres means the bridge is unsafe.","High-strength concrete alone prevents reinforcement corrosion in seawater.","Hong Kong Highways Department data state that Stonecutters Bridge can deflect about 1.8 m at mid-span under traffic and about 2.2 m under wind."],"answer":2,"explanation":"香港路政署公開資料指出，昂船洲大橋跨中在交通荷載下撓度可達約 1.8 m，在風荷載下可達約 2.2 m。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hong Kong Highways Department data state that Stonecutters Bridge can deflect about 1.8 m at mid-span under traffic and about 2.2 m under wind. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b009-v13-30","title":"跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「跨中 GNSS 測點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mid-span GNSS stations” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：撓跨比：交通 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566，風 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463。若 GNSS 定位精度 ±15 mm，相對交通撓度的量測誤差約 15/1,800 ≈ 0.8%，足以追蹤 5% 量級的勁度變化。精度為教學假設，撓度為公開資料。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Deflection-to-span ratios are 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566 for traffic and 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463 for wind. With ±15 mm GNSS precision, the error relative to the traffic deflection is about 15/1,800 ≈ 0.8%, enough to track stiffness changes of the order of 5%. The precision is a teaching assumption; the deflections are published values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以動態地磅或交通攝影辨識重車事件，計算單位車重的撓度影響線並與模型比較；以颱風事件資料比對風速—撓度曲線；感測器每年校正，GNSS 基準站設在穩定地點，並與精密水準定期比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify heavy-vehicle events with weigh-in-motion or traffic cameras, compute deflection influence lines per unit vehicle weight and compare with the model; compare wind speed–deflection curves from typhoon records; calibrate sensors yearly, place the GNSS reference station on stable ground and cross-check periodically with precise levelling.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"撓跨比：交通 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566，風 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463。若 GNSS 定位精度 ±15 mm，相對交通撓度的量測誤差約 15/1,800 ≈ 0.8%，足以追蹤 5% 量級的勁度變化。精度為教學假設，撓度為公開資料。","textEn":"Deflection-to-span ratios are 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566 for traffic and 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463 for wind. With ±15 mm GNSS precision, the error relative to the traffic deflection is about 15/1,800 ≈ 0.8%, enough to track stiffness changes of the order of 5%. The precision is a teaching assumption; the deflections are published values.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation\", which statement holds?","options":["撓跨比：交通 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566，風 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463。","橋面越寬越重，風就越吹不動，所以千米跨只要加重即可抗颱風。","不鏽鋼外皮只是為了外觀好看，不參與結構受力。"],"optionsEn":["Deflection-to-span ratios are 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566 for traffic and 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463 for wind.","A wider, heavier deck is always harder for wind to move, so a 1 km span only needs more weight to resist typhoons.","The stainless skin is only for appearance and carries no structural load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"撓跨比：交通 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566，風 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Deflection-to-span ratios are 1.8/1,018 ≈ 1/566 for traffic and 2.2/1,018 ≈ 1/463 for wind. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b009-v13-31","title":"跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「跨中 GNSS 測點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mid-span GNSS stations” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以動態地磅或交通攝影辨識重車事件，計算單位車重的撓度影響線並與模型比較；以颱風事件資料比對風速—撓度曲線；感測器每年校正，GNSS 基準站設在穩定地點，並與精密水準定期比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify heavy-vehicle events with weigh-in-motion or traffic cameras, compute deflection influence lines per unit vehicle weight and compare with the model; compare wind speed–deflection curves from typhoon records; calibrate sensors yearly, place the GNSS reference station on stable ground and cross-check periodically with precise levelling. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：監測報告要以「荷載分類後的殘差趨勢」呈現，而不是原始讀數；警戒值應依設計預測加上量測不確定度設定，並寫明超限時的通報對象與現場複核程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: Monitoring reports should present residual trends after load classification, not raw readings; alert levels should be set from design predictions plus measurement uncertainty, stating who is notified and how field verification proceeds when exceeded.","failure":"注意干擾：若把颱風或高溫時的大撓度誤判為結構劣化，可能做出不必要的封橋決策；反之若未做溫度與交通分類，真正的勁度下降可能隱藏在日常變動中，直到伸縮縫行程不足才被發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Misreading large typhoon or hot-weather deflections as deterioration can trigger unnecessary closures; without temperature and traffic sorting, a genuine stiffness loss can hide in daily variation until joint travel runs out. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以動態地磅或交通攝影辨識重車事件，計算單位車重的撓度影響線並與模型比較；以颱風事件資料比對風速—撓度曲線；感測器每年校正，GNSS 基準站設在穩定地點，並與精密水準定期比對。","textEn":"Identify heavy-vehicle events with weigh-in-motion or traffic cameras, compute deflection influence lines per unit vehicle weight and compare with the model; compare wind speed–deflection curves from typhoon records; calibrate sensors yearly, place the GNSS reference station on stable ground and cross-check periodically with precise levelling.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"監測報告要以「荷載分類後的殘差趨勢」呈現，而不是原始讀數；警戒值應依設計預測加上量測不確定度設定，並寫明超限時的通報對象與現場複核程序。","textEn":"Monitoring reports should present residual trends after load classification, not raw readings; alert levels should be set from design predictions plus measurement uncertainty, stating who is notified and how field verification proceeds when exceeded.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以動態地磅或交通攝影辨識重車事件，計算單位車重的撓度影響線並與模型比較。","成橋狀態能抗颱風，施工中的懸臂狀態自然也能。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Identify heavy-vehicle events with weigh-in-motion or traffic cameras, compute deflection influence lines per unit vehicle weight and compare with the model.","If the completed bridge resists typhoons, the cantilever stage naturally does too."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以動態地磅或交通攝影辨識重車事件，計算單位車重的撓度影響線並與模型比較；以颱風事件資料比對風速—撓度曲線；感測器每年校正，GNSS 基準站設在穩定地點，並與精密水準定期比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify heavy-vehicle events with weigh-in-motion or traffic cameras, compute deflection influence lines per unit vehicle weight and compare with the model; compare wind speed–deflection curves from typhoon records; calibrate sensors yearly, place the GNSS reference station on stable ground and cross-check periodically with precise levelling. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b009-v13-32","title":"跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「跨中 GNSS 測點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mid-span GNSS stations” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把颱風或高溫時的大撓度誤判為結構劣化，可能做出不必要的封橋決策；反之若未做溫度與交通分類，真正的勁度下降可能隱藏在日常變動中，直到伸縮縫行程不足才被發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Misreading large typhoon or hot-weather deflections as deterioration can trigger unnecessary closures; without temperature and traffic sorting, a genuine stiffness loss can hide in daily variation until joint travel runs out. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：監測系統以 GNSS、加速度計、應變計、溫度計與風速計記錄橋梁反應，工程師要把實測撓度依溫度、交通與風況分類，才能和設計預測公平比較，並從長期趨勢找出支承卡滯、索力變化或基礎沉陷的徵兆。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The monitoring system records response with GNSS, accelerometers, strain gauges, thermometers and anemometers, and engineers must sort measured deflections by temperature, traffic and wind before comparing them fairly with predictions, then look for signs of seized bearings, stay-force change or foundation settlement in long-term trends.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「大橋跨中撓度達到一兩公尺，就表示結構不安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A mid-span deflection of one or two metres means the bridge is unsafe.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把颱風或高溫時的大撓度誤判為結構劣化，可能做出不必要的封橋決策；反之若未做溫度與交通分類，真正的勁度下降可能隱藏在日常變動中，直到伸縮縫行程不足才被發現。","textEn":"Misreading large typhoon or hot-weather deflections as deterioration can trigger unnecessary closures; without temperature and traffic sorting, a genuine stiffness loss can hide in daily variation until joint travel runs out.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨中撓度與結構健康監測判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mid-span deflection and health-monitoring interpretation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要混凝土強度高，海水環境下就不會有鋼筋腐蝕問題。","若把颱風或高溫時的大撓度誤判為結構劣化，可能做出不必要的封橋決策；反之若未做溫度與交通分類，真正的勁度下降可能隱藏在日常變動中，直到伸縮縫行程不足才被發現。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","High-strength concrete alone prevents reinforcement corrosion in seawater.","Misreading large typhoon or hot-weather deflections as deterioration can trigger unnecessary closures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若把颱風或高溫時的大撓度誤判為結構劣化，可能做出不必要的封橋決策；反之若未做溫度與交通分類，真正的勁度下降可能隱藏在日常變動中，直到伸縮縫行程不足才被發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Misreading large typhoon or hot-weather deflections as deterioration can trigger unnecessary closures; without temperature and traffic sorting, a genuine stiffness loss can hide in daily variation until joint travel runs out. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b009-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計」與「長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting\" and \"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b009-v13-33","title":"海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「下塔不鏽鋼鋼筋」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stainless reinforcement in the lower tower” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"昂船洲大橋下塔位於海水飛濺與潮汐乾濕交替區，氯離子是鋼筋腐蝕的主要驅動力。公開資料指出下塔為使用不鏽鋼鋼筋的鋼筋混凝土，基礎為擴底鑽掘樁，岩盤深度約在 −40 m 至 −90 m 之間，並考慮負摩擦力。氯離子由表面向內擴散，到達鋼筋位置且濃度超過臨界值後，碳鋼鋼筋開始腐蝕並膨脹剝落；不鏽鋼鋼筋的臨界氯離子濃度高得多，可大幅延後腐蝕起始，適合用在最難維修的高風險區。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「下塔不鏽鋼鋼筋」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Stonecutters lower towers sit in the seawater splash and tidal zone, where chloride drives reinforcement corrosion. Published data state the lower towers are reinforced concrete with stainless steel bars, and the foundations are bored piles with enlarged bases, with bedrock at roughly −40 m to −90 m and negative skin friction considered. Chlorides diffuse inward from the surface, and once they reach the bars above a threshold, carbon-steel bars start corroding, expand and spall the cover; stainless bars tolerate a much higher chloride threshold, greatly delaying corrosion onset, which suits the highest-risk zones that are hardest to repair. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Stainless reinforcement in the lower tower” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：氯離子前緣深度約 x ≈ 2√(D·t)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The chloride front depth is roughly x ≈ 2√(D·t).","failure":"常見誤解：「只要混凝土強度高，海水環境下就不會有鋼筋腐蝕問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High-strength concrete alone prevents reinforcement corrosion in seawater.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「下塔不鏽鋼鋼筋」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Stainless reinforcement in the lower tower”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-33-k1","title":"海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計","titleEn":"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting","text":"昂船洲大橋下塔位於海水飛濺與潮汐乾濕交替區，氯離子是鋼筋腐蝕的主要驅動力。公開資料指出下塔為使用不鏽鋼鋼筋的鋼筋混凝土，基礎為擴底鑽掘樁，岩盤深度約在 −40 m 至 −90 m 之間，並考慮負摩擦力。","textEn":"The Stonecutters lower towers sit in the seawater splash and tidal zone, where chloride drives reinforcement corrosion. Published data state the lower towers are reinforced concrete with stainless steel bars, and the foundations are bored piles with enlarged bases, with bedrock at roughly −40 m to −90 m and negative skin friction considered.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要混凝土強度高，海水環境下就不會有鋼筋腐蝕問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High-strength concrete alone prevents reinforcement corrosion in seawater. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting\" is correct?","options":["昂船洲大橋下塔位於海水飛濺與潮汐乾濕交替區，氯離子是鋼筋腐蝕的主要驅動力。","只要混凝土強度高，海水環境下就不會有鋼筋腐蝕問題。","斜拉索索力一旦施工完成就不會再改變，不需要追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["The Stonecutters lower towers sit in the seawater splash and tidal zone, where chloride drives reinforcement corrosion.","High-strength concrete alone prevents reinforcement corrosion in seawater.","Stay forces never change after construction, so they need no tracking."],"answer":0,"explanation":"昂船洲大橋下塔位於海水飛濺與潮汐乾濕交替區，氯離子是鋼筋腐蝕的主要驅動力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Stonecutters lower towers sit in the seawater splash and tidal zone, where chloride drives reinforcement corrosion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b009-v13-34","title":"海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計：定量估算","titleEn":"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「下塔不鏽鋼鋼筋」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stainless reinforcement in the lower tower” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：氯離子前緣深度約 x ≈ 2√(D·t)。取 D = 1×10⁻¹² m²/s、t = 120 年（約 3.79×10⁹ s）：x ≈ 2√(3.79×10⁻³) ≈ 0.123 m；若以低滲透混凝土使 D = 3×10⁻¹³ m²/s，x ≈ 0.067 m。前者已超過 75 mm 保護層，說明需搭配不鏽鋼鋼筋或更低滲透率。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The chloride front depth is roughly x ≈ 2√(D·t). With D = 1×10⁻¹² m²/s and t = 120 years (about 3.79×10⁹ s), x ≈ 2√(3.79×10⁻³) ≈ 0.123 m; a low-permeability concrete with D = 3×10⁻¹³ m²/s gives x ≈ 0.067 m. The first exceeds a 75 mm cover, showing the need for stainless bars or lower permeability. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：施工時以試體量測氯離子擴散係數與保護層厚度（鋼筋掃描儀），營運期定期鑽取粉末或岩心量測氯離子剖面，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，推估腐蝕起始時間；基礎則以沉陷監測與水下檢查確認。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: During construction measure chloride diffusion on specimens and cover with a covermeter; in service periodically sample dust or cores for chloride profiles, fit surface concentration and diffusion coefficient and project corrosion onset; check foundations with settlement monitoring and underwater inspection.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"氯離子前緣深度約 x ≈ 2√(D·t)。取 D = 1×10⁻¹² m²/s、t = 120 年（約 3.79×10⁹ s）：x ≈ 2√(3.79×10⁻³) ≈ 0.123 m；若以低滲透混凝土使 D = 3×10⁻¹³ m²/s，x ≈ 0.067 m。前者已超過 75 mm 保護層，說明需搭配不鏽鋼鋼筋或更低滲透率。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The chloride front depth is roughly x ≈ 2√(D·t). With D = 1×10⁻¹² m²/s and t = 120 years (about 3.79×10⁹ s), x ≈ 2√(3.79×10⁻³) ≈ 0.123 m; a low-permeability concrete with D = 3×10⁻¹³ m²/s gives x ≈ 0.067 m. The first exceeds a 75 mm cover, showing the need for stainless bars or lower permeability. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting\", which statement holds?","options":["塔梁之間只要用固定支承鎖死，橋就最穩。","氯離子前緣深度約 x ≈ 2√(D·t)。","同一座橋的斜拉索應該都一樣粗，才方便施工和維護。"],"optionsEn":["Fixing the deck rigidly to the tower always makes the bridge most stable.","The chloride front depth is roughly x ≈ 2√(D·t).","All stays on one bridge should have the same size for easier construction and maintenance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"氯離子前緣深度約 x ≈ 2√(D·t)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The chloride front depth is roughly x ≈ 2√(D·t). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b009-v13-35","title":"海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「下塔不鏽鋼鋼筋」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stainless reinforcement in the lower tower” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"施工時以試體量測氯離子擴散係數與保護層厚度（鋼筋掃描儀），營運期定期鑽取粉末或岩心量測氯離子剖面，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，推估腐蝕起始時間；基礎則以沉陷監測與水下檢查確認。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"During construction measure chloride diffusion on specimens and cover with a covermeter; in service periodically sample dust or cores for chloride profiles, fit surface concentration and diffusion coefficient and project corrosion onset; check foundations with settlement monitoring and underwater inspection. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：耐久設計報告要依暴露分區列出保護層、混凝土配比、鋼筋材質與設計年限內的腐蝕起始推估，並在交接時提供監測取樣位置圖，使後續量測能在相同位置重複比較。","observationEn":"Site practice: The durability report should list cover, mix, bar type and projected corrosion onset within the design life for each exposure zone, and handover should include a sampling-location map so later measurements repeat at the same spots.","failure":"注意干擾：飛濺區保護層不足或混凝土蜂窩，會讓氯離子提早到達鋼筋，造成鏽脹裂縫與剝落；若不同材質鋼筋混用而未隔離，接觸處也可能加速碳鋼腐蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Insufficient cover or honeycombing in the splash zone lets chlorides reach the bars early, causing rust cracking and spalling; mixing reinforcement types without isolation can accelerate carbon-steel corrosion at contacts. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"施工時以試體量測氯離子擴散係數與保護層厚度（鋼筋掃描儀），營運期定期鑽取粉末或岩心量測氯離子剖面，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，推估腐蝕起始時間；基礎則以沉陷監測與水下檢查確認。","textEn":"During construction measure chloride diffusion on specimens and cover with a covermeter; in service periodically sample dust or cores for chloride profiles, fit surface concentration and diffusion coefficient and project corrosion onset; check foundations with settlement monitoring and underwater inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"耐久設計報告要依暴露分區列出保護層、混凝土配比、鋼筋材質與設計年限內的腐蝕起始推估，並在交接時提供監測取樣位置圖，使後續量測能在相同位置重複比較。","textEn":"The durability report should list cover, mix, bar type and projected corrosion onset within the design life for each exposure zone, and handover should include a sampling-location map so later measurements repeat at the same spots.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","鋼梁與混凝土梁只要用螺栓頭對頭接上，力量就會平均傳遞。","施工時以試體量測氯離子擴散係數與保護層厚度（鋼筋掃描儀），營運期定期鑽取粉末或岩心量測氯離子剖面，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，推估腐蝕起始時間。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Bolting the steel girder end to the concrete girder end transfers force evenly.","During construction measure chloride diffusion on specimens and cover with a covermeter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"施工時以試體量測氯離子擴散係數與保護層厚度（鋼筋掃描儀），營運期定期鑽取粉末或岩心量測氯離子剖面，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，推估腐蝕起始時間；基礎則以沉陷監測與水下檢查確認。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"During construction measure chloride diffusion on specimens and cover with a covermeter; in service periodically sample dust or cores for chloride profiles, fit surface concentration and diffusion coefficient and project corrosion onset; check foundations with settlement monitoring and underwater inspection. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b009-v13-36","title":"海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計：失效診斷","titleEn":"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「下塔不鏽鋼鋼筋」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stainless reinforcement in the lower tower” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"飛濺區保護層不足或混凝土蜂窩，會讓氯離子提早到達鋼筋，造成鏽脹裂縫與剝落；若不同材質鋼筋混用而未隔離，接觸處也可能加速碳鋼腐蝕。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Insufficient cover or honeycombing in the splash zone lets chlorides reach the bars early, causing rust cracking and spalling; mixing reinforcement types without isolation can accelerate carbon-steel corrosion at contacts. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：氯離子由表面向內擴散，到達鋼筋位置且濃度超過臨界值後，碳鋼鋼筋開始腐蝕並膨脹剝落；不鏽鋼鋼筋的臨界氯離子濃度高得多，可大幅延後腐蝕起始，適合用在最難維修的高風險區。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Chlorides diffuse inward from the surface, and once they reach the bars above a threshold, carbon-steel bars start corroding, expand and spall the cover; stainless bars tolerate a much higher chloride threshold, greatly delaying corrosion onset, which suits the highest-risk zones that are hardest to repair.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要混凝土強度高，海水環境下就不會有鋼筋腐蝕問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High-strength concrete alone prevents reinforcement corrosion in seawater.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"飛濺區保護層不足或混凝土蜂窩，會讓氯離子提早到達鋼筋，造成鏽脹裂縫與剝落；若不同材質鋼筋混用而未隔離，接觸處也可能加速碳鋼腐蝕。","textEn":"Insufficient cover or honeycombing in the splash zone lets chlorides reach the bars early, causing rust cracking and spalling; mixing reinforcement types without isolation can accelerate carbon-steel corrosion at contacts.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「海洋環境下塔與基礎的耐久設計」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Durability of lower towers and foundations in a marine setting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["飛濺區保護層不足或混凝土蜂窩，會讓氯離子提早到達鋼筋，造成鏽脹裂縫與剝落；若不同材質鋼筋混用而未隔離，接觸處也可能加速碳鋼腐蝕。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","斜拉索索力一旦施工完成就不會再改變，不需要追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Insufficient cover or honeycombing in the splash zone lets chlorides reach the bars early, causing rust cracking and spalling.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Stay forces never change after construction, so they need no tracking."],"answer":0,"explanation":"飛濺區保護層不足或混凝土蜂窩，會讓氯離子提早到達鋼筋，造成鏽脹裂縫與剝落；若不同材質鋼筋混用而未隔離，接觸處也可能加速碳鋼腐蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Insufficient cover or honeycombing in the splash zone lets chlorides reach the bars early, causing rust cracking and spalling; mixing reinforcement types without isolation can accelerate carbon-steel corrosion at contacts. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b009-v13-37","title":"長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「540 m 最長索」如何影響昂船洲大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “The 540 m longest stay” governs force, deformation or durability in “Stonecutters Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"最長約 540 m 的斜拉索質量大、垂度明顯，第一振動頻率只有零點幾赫茲，容易受風雨激振，也不易以千斤頂直接量測索力。營運期最實用的方法是以加速度計量測索的自然頻率，再以張緊弦公式換算索力，長索需另行修正垂度與彎曲勁度的影響。定期比對索力趨勢可以發現錨具滑移、鋼線斷絲或阻尼器失效；交接文件則要把每根索的基準頻率、溫度與量測方法完整保存，讓下一代維護工程師能重複同樣的量測。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「540 m 最長索」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The longest stay, about 540 m, is heavy and sags noticeably, with a first natural frequency of only a few tenths of a hertz; it is prone to wind–rain excitation and hard to measure directly with jacks. The most practical in-service method measures the natural frequency with an accelerometer and converts it to force with the taut-string formula, with corrections for sag and bending stiffness on long stays. Comparing force trends over time reveals anchor slip, broken wires or damper failure, and the handover file must preserve each stay’s baseline frequency, temperature and method so the next generation of engineers can repeat the measurement. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “The 540 m longest stay” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：張緊弦 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Taut string f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m).","failure":"常見誤解：「斜拉索索力一旦施工完成就不會再改變，不需要追蹤。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stay forces never change after construction, so they need no tracking.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「540 m 最長索」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “The 540 m longest stay”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-37-k1","title":"長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接","titleEn":"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover","text":"最長約 540 m 的斜拉索質量大、垂度明顯，第一振動頻率只有零點幾赫茲，容易受風雨激振，也不易以千斤頂直接量測索力。營運期最實用的方法是以加速度計量測索的自然頻率，再以張緊弦公式換算索力，長索需另行修正垂度與彎曲勁度的影響。","textEn":"The longest stay, about 540 m, is heavy and sags noticeably, with a first natural frequency of only a few tenths of a hertz; it is prone to wind–rain excitation and hard to measure directly with jacks. The most practical in-service method measures the natural frequency with an accelerometer and converts it to force with the taut-string formula, with corrections for sag and bending stiffness on long stays.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：斜拉索索力一旦施工完成就不會再改變，不需要追蹤。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stay forces never change after construction, so they need no tracking. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover\" is correct?","options":["斜拉索索力一旦施工完成就不會再改變，不需要追蹤。","最長約 540 m 的斜拉索質量大、垂度明顯，第一振動頻率只有零點幾赫茲，容易受風雨激振，也不易以千斤頂直接量測索力。","橋面越寬越重，風就越吹不動，所以千米跨只要加重即可抗颱風。"],"optionsEn":["Stay forces never change after construction, so they need no tracking.","The longest stay, about 540 m, is heavy and sags noticeably, with a first natural frequency of only a few tenths of a hertz.","A wider, heavier deck is always harder for wind to move, so a 1 km span only needs more weight to resist typhoons."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最長約 540 m 的斜拉索質量大、垂度明顯，第一振動頻率只有零點幾赫茲，容易受風雨激振，也不易以千斤頂直接量測索力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The longest stay, about 540 m, is heavy and sags noticeably, with a first natural frequency of only a few tenths of a hertz; it is prone to wind–rain excitation and hard to measure directly with jacks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b009-v13-38","title":"長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「540 m 最長索」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “The 540 m longest stay” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：張緊弦 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。取 L = 540 m、m = 70,000/540 ≈ 129.6 kg/m、T = 9,000 kN：√(9×10⁶/129.6) ≈ 263.5 m/s，f₁ ≈ 263.5/1,080 ≈ 0.244 Hz；若索力降 10%，f₁ 只降到約 0.231 Hz（√0.9 ≈ 0.949），量測需要足夠的頻率解析度。索力為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Taut string f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m). With L = 540 m, m = 70,000/540 ≈ 129.6 kg/m and T = 9,000 kN, √(9×10⁶/129.6) ≈ 263.5 m/s and f₁ ≈ 263.5/1,080 ≈ 0.244 Hz; a 10% force loss lowers f₁ only to about 0.231 Hz (√0.9 ≈ 0.949), so adequate frequency resolution is essential. The force is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每根索以至少約 10 分鐘的環境振動紀錄取得多階頻率，以高階頻率比值檢查垂度與彎曲勁度修正，再與施工完成時以千斤頂或荷重計標定的索力比較；量測同時記錄索溫與氣溫。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record at least about 10 minutes of ambient vibration per stay to obtain several modal frequencies, use ratios of higher modes to check sag and bending corrections, and compare with forces calibrated by jacks or load cells at completion; record cable and air temperature simultaneously.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"張緊弦 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。取 L = 540 m、m = 70,000/540 ≈ 129.6 kg/m、T = 9,000 kN：√(9×10⁶/129.6) ≈ 263.5 m/s，f₁ ≈ 263.5/1,080 ≈ 0.244 Hz；若索力降 10%，f₁ 只降到約 0.231 Hz（√0.9 ≈ 0.949），量測需要足夠的頻率解析度。索力為教學假設。","textEn":"Taut string f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m). With L = 540 m, m = 70,000/540 ≈ 129.6 kg/m and T = 9,000 kN, √(9×10⁶/129.6) ≈ 263.5 m/s and f₁ ≈ 263.5/1,080 ≈ 0.244 Hz; a 10% force loss lowers f₁ only to about 0.231 Hz (√0.9 ≈ 0.949), so adequate frequency resolution is essential. The force is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["不鏽鋼外皮只是為了外觀好看，不參與結構受力。","成橋狀態能抗颱風，施工中的懸臂狀態自然也能。","張緊弦 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。"],"optionsEn":["The stainless skin is only for appearance and carries no structural load.","If the completed bridge resists typhoons, the cantilever stage naturally does too.","Taut string f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"張緊弦 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Taut string f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b009-v13-39","title":"長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「540 m 最長索」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “The 540 m longest stay” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每根索以至少約 10 分鐘的環境振動紀錄取得多階頻率，以高階頻率比值檢查垂度與彎曲勁度修正，再與施工完成時以千斤頂或荷重計標定的索力比較；量測同時記錄索溫與氣溫。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record at least about 10 minutes of ambient vibration per stay to obtain several modal frequencies, use ratios of higher modes to check sag and bending corrections, and compare with forces calibrated by jacks or load cells at completion; record cable and air temperature simultaneously. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接資料應包含每根索的基準頻率表、計算參數（長度、單位質量、垂度修正）、量測位置與照片；維護單位每次量測都要沿用相同程序，差異超過警戒時先複測再啟動調查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover data should include a baseline frequency table for every stay, calculation parameters (length, mass per metre, sag correction), measurement locations and photographs; the maintainer must follow the same procedure each time and repeat a measurement before launching an investigation when a deviation exceeds the alert level.","failure":"注意干擾：只用第一頻率而不修正垂度，長索索力可能被高估或低估數個百分點，使真正的錨具滑移被誤判；量測時段若遇陣風或交通激振，頻譜出現交雜峰值，也會造成錯誤判讀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using only the first frequency without sag correction can mis-estimate long-stay force by several percent and mask real anchor slip; gusts or traffic excitation during the record add confusing spectral peaks and lead to misreading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每根索以至少約 10 分鐘的環境振動紀錄取得多階頻率，以高階頻率比值檢查垂度與彎曲勁度修正，再與施工完成時以千斤頂或荷重計標定的索力比較；量測同時記錄索溫與氣溫。","textEn":"Record at least about 10 minutes of ambient vibration per stay to obtain several modal frequencies, use ratios of higher modes to check sag and bending corrections, and compare with forces calibrated by jacks or load cells at completion; record cable and air temperature simultaneously.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接資料應包含每根索的基準頻率表、計算參數（長度、單位質量、垂度修正）、量測位置與照片；維護單位每次量測都要沿用相同程序，差異超過警戒時先複測再啟動調查。","textEn":"Handover data should include a baseline frequency table for every stay, calculation parameters (length, mass per metre, sag correction), measurement locations and photographs; the maintainer must follow the same procedure each time and repeat a measurement before launching an investigation when a deviation exceeds the alert level.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover\"?","options":["每根索以至少約 10 分鐘的環境振動紀錄取得多階頻率，以高階頻率比值檢查垂度與彎曲勁度修正，再與施工完成時以千斤頂或荷重計標定的索力比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","風洞模型只要幾何縮尺正確，試驗結果就能直接放大套用到實橋。"],"optionsEn":["Record at least about 10 minutes of ambient vibration per stay to obtain several modal frequencies, use ratios of higher modes to check sag and bending corrections, and compare with forces calibrated by jacks or load cells at completion.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If a wind-tunnel model is geometrically correct, its results scale directly to the full bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每根索以至少約 10 分鐘的環境振動紀錄取得多階頻率，以高階頻率比值檢查垂度與彎曲勁度修正，再與施工完成時以千斤頂或荷重計標定的索力比較；量測同時記錄索溫與氣溫。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record at least about 10 minutes of ambient vibration per stay to obtain several modal frequencies, use ratios of higher modes to check sag and bending corrections, and compare with forces calibrated by jacks or load cells at completion; record cable and air temperature simultaneously. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b009-v13-40","title":"長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"prerequisiteIds":["b009-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「540 m 最長索」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “The 540 m longest stay” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用第一頻率而不修正垂度，長索索力可能被高估或低估數個百分點，使真正的錨具滑移被誤判；量測時段若遇陣風或交通激振，頻譜出現交雜峰值，也會造成錯誤判讀。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using only the first frequency without sag correction can mis-estimate long-stay force by several percent and mask real anchor slip; gusts or traffic excitation during the record add confusing spectral peaks and lead to misreading. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：定期比對索力趨勢可以發現錨具滑移、鋼線斷絲或阻尼器失效；交接文件則要把每根索的基準頻率、溫度與量測方法完整保存，讓下一代維護工程師能重複同樣的量測。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Comparing force trends over time reveals anchor slip, broken wires or damper failure, and the handover file must preserve each stay’s baseline frequency, temperature and method so the next generation of engineers can repeat the measurement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「斜拉索索力一旦施工完成就不會再改變，不需要追蹤。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stay forces never change after construction, so they need no tracking.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b009-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用第一頻率而不修正垂度，長索索力可能被高估或低估數個百分點，使真正的錨具滑移被誤判；量測時段若遇陣風或交通激振，頻譜出現交雜峰值，也會造成錯誤判讀。","textEn":"Using only the first frequency without sag correction can mis-estimate long-stay force by several percent and mask real anchor slip; gusts or traffic excitation during the record add confusing spectral peaks and lead to misreading.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]},{"id":"b009-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長索頻率、索力追蹤與維護交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long-stay frequency, force tracking and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只用第一頻率而不修正垂度，長索索力可能被高估或低估數個百分點，使真正的錨具滑移被誤判；量測時段若遇陣風或交通激振，頻譜出現交雜峰值，也會造成錯誤判讀。","橋面越寬越重，風就越吹不動，所以千米跨只要加重即可抗颱風。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using only the first frequency without sag correction can mis-estimate long-stay force by several percent and mask real anchor slip.","A wider, heavier deck is always harder for wind to move, so a 1 km span only needs more weight to resist typhoons."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只用第一頻率而不修正垂度，長索索力可能被高估或低估數個百分點，使真正的錨具滑移被誤判；量測時段若遇陣風或交通激振，頻譜出現交雜峰值，也會造成錯誤判讀。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using only the first frequency without sag correction can mis-estimate long-stay force by several percent and mask real anchor slip; gusts or traffic excitation during the record add confusing spectral peaks and lead to misreading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-hyd-stonecutters-factsheet","v13s-afgc-stonecutters-design","v13s-istructe-stonecutters-2010","v13s-jsce-tanaka-stonecutters"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
